'' =====================================================================
''
''   File....... test-o29c-setq-block-workaround.spin2
''   Purpose.... Hardware-verification rig, O29 follow-up: does E8's
''               workaround (k NOPs between a no-wait RDFAST and the next
''               hub instruction) protect a SETQ block RDLONG?  And what
''               does a single released block read at k = 0 do to the
''               block, to cog RAM and to the cog?
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 1 Oct 2026
''
'' =====================================================================

{ WHAT IS ALREADY MEASURED (Rev C silicon, 200 MHz)

  EF-084: after a no-wait RDFAST (D = $8000_0000), a RDLONG issued at once
  (k = 0 NOPs between them) that waits for its own hub slot is released
  when the stream's first long reaches the FIFO, and writes its
  destination with the long of the PREVIOUS slow hub read (the primer).
  With the primer at slot bits 0 this happened in 43 of the 64 (af, ar)
  cells, by delta = (ar - af) mod 8 as 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2, identical in all
  16 repetitions; 7 NOPs (k = 7) between the two gave zero.  The cell map
  at k = 0 (row af, position ar; P released, S correct):
    af0 PPPSSSSS  af1 SPPSSSSS  af2 PPPPPPPP  af3 PPPPPPPP
    af4 PPPSPPPP  af5 PPPSSPPP  af6 PPPSSSPP  af7 PPPSSSSP
  EF-086 (the SETQ block arm of the O29B rig): "setq #7" + "rdlong" of 8
  longs into a sacrificial cog-register range.  NOP control and waiting
  form: the right block in 1024 of 1024 records, 0 cog registers changed
  outside the sacrificial range.  No-wait RDFAST at k = 0: the first trial
  (af 0, ar 0, repetition 0) recorded the primer $A5A5_0001 in block long
  0 and longs 1-7 still at the seed (not written by the read); the
  measuring cog then did not finish the run within 1 s and was stopped
  (COGSTOP); 1,023 records were never written.  k = 7 never ran.

WHAT THIS RIG DECIDES, ONE ARM EACH, IN THIS ORDER
  Each arm prints its rows, its gate and its verdicts as soon as it
  completes, before the next arm starts.  The characterisation arm (arm 1)
  runs BEFORE the workaround arm (arm 2): it is the workaround arm's
  positive control for block release.  Every trial and run of both arms
  has its own fresh measuring cog, so nothing one of them does to a cog
  carries into the next.

  ARM 0  POSITIVE CONTROL.  C1, PS, T1 at k = 0 and T1 at k = 7, exactly
         the O29 construction, on one measuring cog.  MUST reproduce
         EF-084 (the map above: 43 per repetition, delta split 8 8 7 6 5 4
         3 2, k = 7 zero), else RIG FAIL and no later verdict counts.
  ARM 1  CHARACTERISATION AT k = 0 (RECORDS; the positive control for block
         release).  Single trials, each in its own fresh cog, per cell one
         NOP control trial (QS N) and 4 no-wait RDFAST trials at k = 0
         (QS T).  Cells, with their class in the EF-084 map above:
           af0 ar0   released (P)        af2 ar0   released (P)
           af0 ar4   escaping (S)        af1 ar3   escaping (S)
         Per trial: the 8 block longs as recorded right after the trial;
         whether the cog completed the trial (done within 1 s); whether it
         then answered a PING within 100 ms; and, if it answered, which
         cog registers outside the sacrificial range changed since the
         fresh cog's baseline, which registers outside the sacrificial
         range hold a block or primer long, and the sacrificial range as
         it stood at the ping.
         MUST (controls): the right block, completed, answered, 0
         registers changed, no block or primer long outside the
         sacrificial range; else the arm's gate fails.
         RELEASE SHOWN: at least one released-cell test trial whose block
         has the primer in long 0, or a long left unwritten (still the
         seed, or the record fill), or whose cog did not finish within 1 s
         (stopped).
         OBSERVED O29C SETQ k0: the escaping-cell trials with the right
         block; the released-cell trials by block pattern (right block /
         long 0 the primer and longs 1-7 still the seed / other); the
         trials completed; the trials where the cog answered afterwards;
         RELEASE SHOWN yes / no; then one line per cell, and one line of
         register changes.  Records only: never CONFIRMED or REFUTED.
         FIFO HISTORY.  A fresh cog's FIFO history differs from the O29B
         run (EF-086), in which the block release was followed by the cog
         not finishing.  So this arm may not reproduce that outcome; it
         records whatever happens.
  ARM 2  BLOCK READ, WORKAROUND RUNS.  Every run in a FRESH measuring cog
         (below).  "setq #7" + "rdlong blk0, pr" reads 8 longs into the
         8 sacrificial registers; SETQ sits directly before its RDLONG,
         so the k NOPs sit between the RDFAST and the SETQ.
           QB N k0  NOP in place of the RDFAST (control)
           QB C k0  waiting RDFAST (D = 0), then setq + rdlong
           QB T k6  no-wait RDFAST, 6 NOPs, setq + rdlong
           QB T k7  no-wait RDFAST, 7 NOPs, setq + rdlong
           QB T k8  no-wait RDFAST, 8 NOPs, setq + rdlong
         E8's rule: 16 clocks, or 7 non-hub instructions, from the no-wait
         RDFAST to the next hub instruction.  SETQ is a non-hub
         instruction, so k6 (6 NOPs + SETQ) is exactly the rule as written;
         k7 and k8 show margin.
         CLOCKS from the start of the RDFAST to the start of the block
         RDLONG (cog execution: RDFAST with D[31] = 1 takes 2 clocks, P2
         Documentation, FIFO section; NOP and SETQ take 2 clocks each):
           QB T k6   2 + 6 x 2 + 2 = 16 clocks (E8's rule exactly)
           QB T k7   2 + 7 x 2 + 2 = 18 clocks
           QB T k8   2 + 8 x 2 + 2 = 20 clocks
           QB C k0   the waiting RDFAST's own wait (it waits until the
                     FIFO has begun receiving hub data) + 2 (SETQ)
           for comparison, T1 (no SETQ): 2 + 2k, so T1 k7 = 16 clocks
         Verified from the listing: in each block copy the RDFAST, the k
         NOPs, the SETQ and the RDLONG sit at consecutive cog addresses
         (VERIFIED OPCODES below), and every one of them is a fixed
         2-clock instruction except the waiting RDFAST.
         MUST (QB N k0): the right block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024
         records, 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range,
         no block or primer long outside it, and the cog completes the
         run; else the arm's gate fails.
         PREDICT (QB C k0, QB T k6, QB T k7, QB T k8), written before the
         run:
           (a) the right block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024 records;
           (b) 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range and
               the loop variables, and no block or primer long found in
               any register outside the sacrificial range;
           (c) the cog completes the run (done within 1 s, mode echo
               right, the integrity copy arrives).
         POSITIVE CONTROL FOR RELEASE (arm 1, which runs first): a clean
         workaround run proves something only if the same rig, in the
         same run, shows a block read being released.  So CONFIRMED needs
         arm 1's RELEASE SHOWN and arm 1's gate passed.
         VERDICT O29C BLOCK WAITING: / BLOCK k6: / BLOCK k7: / BLOCK k8:
           CONFIRMED if (a), (b) and (c) all hold, arm 1 showed a release
           and arm 1's gate passed.
           INCONCLUSIVE in place of CONFIRMED if arm 1 showed no release:
           "the rig did not show a block read being released
           (characterisation arm), so a clean workaround run proves
           nothing"; or if arm 1's gate failed.
           REFUTED naming each part that failed: "wrong long" (records
           written with a long that is not the right block), "register
           change" (b fails), "did not finish within 1 s (stopped)" (c
           fails; a stalled cog and a slow one look the same).  A REFUTED
           stands whatever arm 1 showed: a failing run needs no positive
           control.
           INCONCLUSIVE if no part failed but one could not be read (the
           cog completed but no integrity copy arrived).

FRESH MEASURING COG PER RUN (arms 1 and 2)
  Before each trial (arm 1) or run (arm 2) cog 0 starts a measuring cog
  (COGINIT, cog execution, start-up handshake within 1 s) and has it copy
  its cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub (the baseline, checked against the loaded
  image outside the loop variables).  Then it sends the run, waits up to
  1 s, and stops the cog (COGSTOP) whether or not it finished.  A run
  whose cog does not finish loses only that run: its records so far are
  printed (U = never written) and the next run starts a fresh cog.  A cog
  that does not start, or does not answer its baseline command, is
  stopped and that run is reported NOT RUN; the next run tries again.
  Arm 0's cog is stopped at the end of arm 0.
  FIFO PRE-CONDITIONING.  Every measuring cog, before its start-up
  handshake, issues a blocking "rdfast #0, stream" and a settle loop.  So
  the first trial of every run starts, like every later trial, with the
  FIFO in read mode streaming from the stream region, full and idle; a
  fresh cog's first RDFAST is not its first FIFO use.
  PING (arm 1).  After a completed trial cog 0 sends CMD_PING: the cog
  copies its cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub, writes $0000_0B22 to the mailbox
  and clears its command.  "Answered" = command cleared within 100 ms and
  $0000_0B22 written.  A trial that did not complete is not pinged.

INTEGRITY
  The sacrificial range sits between two 8-long guard bands of constants
  at the top of the cog image, so an overrun in either direction changes
  a checked register.  A copy is compared with the same cog's baseline:
  every changed register outside the sacrificial range and the loop
  variables is listed (first 16) and counted.  Separately, every register
  outside the sacrificial range (loop variables included) that changed and
  now holds a block-source long ($5A5A_0100..$5A5A_010E) or the primer is
  listed and counted, except the primer in c_tmp, the primer read's own
  destination.
  LIMITS.  The check sees the final cog-RAM state only (a register
  changed and changed back is not seen).  A loop variable changes by
  design, so its corruption is detected only when the stray value is a
  block or primer long.  Registers $1F0-$1FF are not copied.

STATED DEVIATION FROM THE STUDY'S HARNESS NOTE (as O29)
  This rig compiles WITH debug (pnut-ts -d) and confines the debugger to
  cog 0 (DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001).  The measuring cog has no debug
  interrupt, no debug() and no BRK, and sets up no interrupt; EF-084 and
  EF-086 ran exactly this way.

RIG
  Bare P2 board, 200 MHz.  No pins, no jumpers, no instruments.  Cog 0
  (Spin2) fills the hub data, starts measuring cogs, sends one command per
  run, classifies the records from hub RAM and prints them.  The measuring
  cog runs every trial from cog RAM.  After every command the measuring
  cog writes back the FIFO D value it held (MB_ECHO); a mismatch is RIG
  FAIL in arm 0 (the run ends) and a gate failure in arms 1 and 2.
  NOT TESTED: hub execution (P2 Documentation: RDFAST cannot be used in
  hub execution).
  NOT MEASURED: the flags of a block read; the block release map beyond
  the four characterised cells; block reads at distances between k = 0
  and k = 6.

HUB LAYOUT (all below $7_C000; the program image, VAR and cog 0's stack sit
  far below $4_0000, checked at run time before any data is written)
    $4_0000  stream region, 64 longs, long n = $1E1E_0000 + n
    $4_1000  table T: 8 sentinel longs $5A5A_0002, slot bits 0..7
    $4_1200  block source: 15 longs, long i = $5A5A_0100 + i
    $4_3000  primer $A5A5_0001, slot bits 0
    $4_4000  records, up to 8,192 longs, to $4_BFFF
    $4_C000  cog-RAM copy, latest (496 longs); $4_D000 the baseline copy
  Every region starts on a 32-byte boundary, so long n has slot bits n mod
  8.  Cog 0 fills the record area with $EEEE_EEEE before every command, so
  a record the measuring cog never wrote is class U.

ONE TRIAL (measuring cog, cog execution; the timed stretch is the primer,
  the RDFAST (or the NOP standing in for it), exactly k NOPs, and the test
  instruction (SETQ + RDLONG for a block), adjacent, nothing else, no ##)
  image R:  dst := seed $C3C3_0003
            rdlong tmp, primer ; rdfast mode, stream+4*af ; k x nop ;
            rdlong dst, table+4*ar ; settle (>= 200 clk) ; record dst
  block:    blk0..blk7 := seed ; rdlong tmp, primer ; rdfast mode, stream+
            4*af ; k x nop ; setq #7 ; rdlong blk0, block+4*ar ; settle ;
            record blk0..blk7 (setq #7 + wrlong)
  runs: 16 repetitions x 64 cells; record (r*8 + af)*8 + ar.  Arm 1: one
  block trial at the given af, ar; one record.

RECORD CLASSES
  image R  P primer  S sentinel  D seed  F a stream long ($1E1E_0000 + n)
           U $EEEE_EEEE (never written)  X other
  block    . right block  P primer in some longs (rest right)  D seed in
           some longs  M primer and seed  U unwritten  X other
  agree: "." all 16 repetitions identical, else the hex count identical
  to repetition 0.

GATES
  RIG FAIL (harness, ends the run): hub layout, run tables, arm 0's cog
    not starting, a timeout or a mode echo mismatch in arm 0.
  ARM 0: "RIG OK (arm 0 ...)" only if C1 sentinel 1024/1024, PS stream long
    1024/1024, T1 k=0 43 primer by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 in every
    repetition (688 primer + 336 sentinel), T1 k=7 sentinel 1024/1024, no
    U, no X in a control, no disagreeing cell.  Else "RIG FAIL (arm 0
    ...)", and every later verdict prints NO VERDICT.
  ARM 1: "GATE FAIL (arm 1)" for: a NOP control trial not run, not
    completed, not answered, not the right block, or cog RAM not intact;
    a baseline not equal to the loaded image; a mode echo mismatch.  Else
    "GATES PASS (arm 1)".
  ARM 2: "GATE FAIL (arm 2)" for: QB N k0 not run, not completed, not the
    right block in all 1024, or cog RAM not intact; a baseline not equal
    to the loaded image; a mode echo mismatch.  Else "GATES PASS (arm 2)".

VERDICTS (each arm's after its gate; all repeated in the closing summary)
  RIG OK / RIG FAIL                     arm 0
  OBSERVED O29C SETQ k0:                arm 1, records; prefixed NO
    VERDICT when arm 0 or arm 1's gate failed, the raw counts still printed
  VERDICT O29C BLOCK WAITING: / BLOCK k6: / BLOCK k7: / BLOCK k8:
                                        arm 2: NO VERDICT (arm 0 or arm
    2's gate failed; the run did not take place) / CONFIRMED / REFUTED
    (wrong long; register change; did not finish within 1 s (stopped) -
    each named) / INCONCLUSIVE (no release shown in arm 1, or arm 1's
    gate failed; or part (b) unreadable)

VERIFIED OPCODES (pnut-ts -d -l, v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the
  .lst hub image; object offset = cog address * 4 + $1AC).  RDFAST is
  1100011 1LI, RDLONG 1011000 CZI, WRLONG 1100011 0LI, SETQ 1101011 00L
  with S = %000101000, TJNZ 1011100 11I, NOP $0000_0000.
  Cog registers: constants c_strm $0B0, c_res $0B1, c_dump $0B2, c_seedv
  $0B3, c_ready $0B4, c_pong $0B5; loop variables c_cmd $0B6 .. c_tmp $0C7
  (c_mode $0B8, c_pa $0BB, c_one $0C0, c_pf $0C3, c_pr $0C4, c_dst $0C5,
  c_t $0C6, c_tmp $0C7); guard bands $0C8-$0CF and $0D8-$0DF; sacrificial
  range c_blk0 $0D0-$0D7; the image ends at $0DF (pasm_end $0E0).
    rdfast #0,c_strm        $FC7800B0  start-up pre-conditioning (cog $000):
                                       L=1, D=#0, so D[31]=0: BLOCKING
    rdlong c_tmp,c_pa       $FB018EBB  the primer (every copy)
    rdfast c_mode,c_pf      $FC7170C3  L=0 I=0: D[31] is c_mode's value -
                                       $8000_0000 no-wait, 0 waiting (one
                                       encoding serves both forms)
    rdlong c_dst,c_pr       $FB018AC4  the RDLONG under test (arm 0)
    setq #7                 $FD640E28  directly before every block RDLONG
    rdlong c_blk0,c_pr      $FB01A0C4  the block RDLONG (D = $0D0)
    waitx #200 / rflong c_dst   $FD65901F / $FD618A12   PS only
    tjnz c_one,#cmd_done    $FB9D81C4  CMD_B1 exit, after the record
    setq #$1EF / wrlong pasm,c_dump   $FD67DE28 / $FC6000B2   cog-RAM copy
    wrlong c_ready,ptra[MB_ALIVE]     $FC656907   start-up handshake
    wrlong c_pong,ptra[MB_ALIVE]      $FC656B07   the ping's answer
    wrlong c_mode,ptra[MB_ECHO]       $FC657108   mode echo
  No AUGS (##) and no BRK anywhere in the measuring cog: no long of the
  image ($1AC-$52B) has $FF as its top byte or the BRK form.  The O29B
  FIFO flush (a blocking rdfast #0 after every trial) is not kept: no
  WRFAST is issued here.
  Adjacency read from the image (object offsets): primer / RDFAST (or
  NOP) / NOPs / [SETQ] / test:
    tc_r_nop_l   $330, $334 nop, $338 rdlong                       (C1)
    tc_r_rf0_l   $340, $344 rdfast, $348 rdlong                    (T1 k=0)
    tc_r_rf7_l   $350, $354 rdfast, $358-$370 7 nop, $374 rdlong   (T1 k=7)
    tc_r_ps      $37C, $380 rdfast, $384 waitx, $388 rflong        (PS)
    tc_b_nop     $390, $394 nop, $398 setq, $39C rdlong block      (QB N, QS N)
    tc_b_rf0     $3A4, $3A8 rdfast, $3AC setq, $3B0 rdlong block   (QB C, QS T)
    tc_b_rf6     $3B8, $3BC rdfast, $3C0-$3D4 6 nop, $3D8 setq, $3DC rdlong block
    tc_b_rf7     $3E4, $3E8 rdfast, $3EC-$404 7 nop, $408 setq, $40C rdlong block
    tc_b_rf8     $414, $418 rdfast, $41C-$438 8 nop, $43C setq, $440 rdlong block
  So from the start of the RDFAST to the start of the block RDLONG: k6 =
  rdfast + 6 nop + setq = 8 two-clock instructions = 16 clocks (E8's rule:
  7 non-hub instructions); k7 = 9 = 18 clocks; k8 = 10 = 20 clocks; and
  T1 k7 = rdfast + 7 nop = 8 = 16 clocks.  vec_tab ($448) holds $061 $065
  $069 $074 $079 $07E $083 $08E $09A, the cog addresses of the nine copies
  in CP_* order.
  DEBUG OUTPUT.  Every printed line is assembled in lineBuf from hub
  strings and numbers and sent by the ONE debug(zstr_(@lineBuf)) record in
  ln_out(); the only other record is debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION").  The
  listing reports 2 DEBUG records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.

HOW TO RUN
  Compile with pnut-ts -d, load to RAM with DEBUG on (pnut-term-ts, or PNut
  Ctrl-F10).  Runs once; nothing written to flash.  Output: header with
  every prediction, then per arm: its runs or trials (rows + totals), its
  gate line, its verdict lines; then the VERDICT SUMMARY and
  DEBUG_END_SESSION.
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001          ' debug interrupt in cog 0 ONLY (EF-057)

  NSLOT           = 8                   ' slot bits: address bits [4:2]
  NCELL           = NSLOT * NSLOT       ' (af, ar) cells per repetition
  REPS            = 16                  ' repetitions of every cell per run
  NTRIAL          = REPS * NCELL        ' trials per run (1,024)
  BLKN            = 8                   ' longs per SETQ block read (setq #BLKN-1)
  NREC_B          = NTRIAL * BLKN       ' block records per run (8,192 longs)
  SETTLE_N        = 100                 ' DJNZ count of a settle loop: >= 200 clocks
  STREAM_WAIT     = 200                 ' PS: WAITX between the no-wait RDFAST and its RFLONG

  PRIMV           = $A5A5_0001          ' primer: the previous slow hub read
  SENTV           = $5A5A_0002          ' sentinel, table T
  SEEDV           = $C3C3_0003          ' seed: destination before the trial ("never written")
  BLK_V           = $5A5A_0100          ' block source long i = BLK_V + i
  GUARD_V         = $6D6D_0000          ' cog guard-band long i = GUARD_V + i
  STRM_V          = $1E1E_0000          ' stream region long n = STRM_V + n
  UNWRITTEN       = $EEEE_EEEE          ' record-area fill: nothing written here
  FIFO_NO_WAIT    = $8000_0000          ' RDFAST D: D[31]=1 no-wait, block count 0
  FIFO_WAIT       = $0000_0000          ' RDFAST D: D[31]=0 waiting form, block count 0

  T1_PRED         = 43                  ' EF-084: primer cells per repetition at k=0
  T1_PRED_SENT    = NCELL - T1_PRED     ' 21

  ' -- fixed hub layout (HUB LAYOUT in the header) --
  HUB_STRM        = $4_0000
  STRM_LONGS      = 64
  HUB_TBL         = $4_1000
  HUB_BLK         = $4_1200
  BLK_LONGS       = NSLOT + BLKN - 1    ' 15: blocks start at slot bits 0..7
  HUB_PRIM        = $4_3000
  HUB_RES         = $4_4000
  HUB_DUMP        = $4_C000             ' cog-RAM copy written by the measuring cog
  HUB_DUMP0       = $4_D000             ' the baseline copy (cog 0 moves it here)
  COG_DUMP_N      = $1F0                ' cog registers $000-$1EF (496)
  HUB_DATA_LO     = HUB_STRM
  HUB_DATA_END    = HUB_DUMP0 + COG_DUMP_N * 4
  HUB_TOP16K      = $7_C000
  STACK_MARGIN    = $4000

  STAT_READY      = $0000_0A11          ' start-up handshake
  STAT_PONG       = $0000_0B22          ' the answer to a ping
  RUN_TIMEOUT_MS  = 1000                ' a run, a trial, a baseline
  PING_TIMEOUT_MS = 100                 ' arm 2 ping
  LINE_MAX        = 480                 ' longest printed line (chars); longer text is cut
  INT_SHOW        = 16                  ' changed cog registers listed per run or trial

  SUCCESS         = 0
  E_RIG_FAIL      = -1                  ' the measuring cog did not answer in time
  E_MODE_FAIL     = -2                  ' the mode echoed back differs from the mode sent
  E_NO_START      = -3                  ' a measuring cog did not start

CON ' ---- Identifiers ----
  #1, CMD_R, CMD_B, CMD_B1, CMD_SNAP, CMD_PING

  #0, ARM_P, ARM_S, ARM_Q               ' run order: 0, 1 characterisation, 2 workaround
  NARM            = ARM_Q + 1

  #0, SH_R, SH_PS, SH_B                 ' shapes: image R; PS; block
  #0, KD_NOP, KD_PS, KD_WAIT, KD_TEST

  ' trial copies (the measuring cog's vec_tab order)
  #0, CP_R_NOP_L, CP_R_RF0_L, CP_R_RF7_L, CP_R_PS
  #4, CP_B_NOP, CP_B_RF0, CP_B_RF6, CP_B_RF7, CP_B_RF8

  ' run-table fields (runTab, 6 bytes per run)
  #0, RF_ARM, RF_SHAPE, RF_KIND, RF_COPY, RF_NOWAIT, RF_K
  RT_W            = 6

  ' run indexes, in run order
  RUN_C1          = 0
  RUN_PS          = 1
  RUN_T1          = 2                   ' T1 k=0: the reference cell map
  RUN_T1F         = 3                   ' T1 k=7
  RUN_Q           = 4                   ' arm 2: N k0, C k0, T k6, T k7, T k8
  NBRUN           = 5
  NRUN            = RUN_Q + NBRUN
  #0, QS_N, QS_C, QS_T6, QS_T7, QS_T8   ' arm 2 slots

  ' arm 1 trial table (chTab, 4 bytes per trial): kind, af, ar, class in
  ' the EF-084 map (1 released P, 0 escaping S)
  #0, CF_KIND, CF_AF, CF_AR, CF_REL
  CT_W            = 4
  NCELL_S         = 4                   ' characterised cells
  NCH             = NCELL_S * 5         ' per cell 1 NOP control + 4 test trials

  ' state of an arm 2 run or an arm 1 trial
  #0, ST_NOTRUN, ST_NOSTART, ST_NOBASE, ST_LOST, ST_ECHO, ST_DONE

  ' value classes (image R); the block classes share the U/X slots
  #0, VC_PRIM, VC_SENT, VC_SEED, VC_STRM, VC_UNWR, VC_OTHER
  NVC             = VC_OTHER + 1
  #0, BC_OK, BC_PRIM, BC_SEED, BC_MIX
  BC_UNWR         = VC_UNWR
  BC_OTHER        = VC_OTHER

  ' arm 1 block patterns
  #0, PAT_OK, PAT_P1, PAT_OTH

  ' mailbox longs (cog 0 <-> measuring cog)
  #0, MB_CMD, MB_COPY, MB_MODE, MB_AF, MB_AR, MB_PRIM, MB_TBL, MB_ALIVE, MB_ECHO, MB_LEN

VAR ' ---- Rig State ----
  long mbox[MB_LEN]
  long measCog
  byte cellCode[NRUN * NCELL]           ' repetition 0: class
  byte cellAgree[NRUN * NCELL]          ' repetitions identical to repetition 0
  long runCnt[NRUN * NVC]               ' classes over all repetitions
  long runRep0[NRUN * NVC]              ' repetition-0 cells per class
  long runDelta[NRUN * NSLOT]           ' rep 0 by delta: released cells (R: primer, B: primer in the record)
  long runDelta2[NRUN * NSLOT]          ' rep 0 by delta: cells not clean
  long runDisagree[NRUN]
  long runGoodAll[NRUN]                 ' over all repetitions: clean records
  long runOther[NRUN]
  long runOtherVal[NRUN]
  long blkPrim[NBRUN * BLKN]            ' arm 2: primer, per long index, all reps
  long blkSeed[NBRUN * BLKN]
  long blkOth[NBRUN * BLKN]
  long blkOthVal[NBRUN]
  long blkOthIdx[NBRUN]
  long qState[NBRUN]                    ' arm 2: ST_*
  long qBaseOk[NBRUN]
  long intChanged[NBRUN]                ' arm 2: changed cog registers, -1 = no copy arrived
  long intFirst[NBRUN]                  ' arm 2: the first changed register
  long intStray[NBRUN]                  ' arm 2: block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range
  long chRec[NCH * BLKN]                ' arm 1: the block as recorded after the trial
  long chSac[NCH * BLKN]                ' arm 1: the sacrificial range at the ping
  long chState[NCH]
  long chAns[NCH]
  long chBaseOk[NCH]
  long chChanged[NCH]
  long chStray[NCH]
  long armDamage[NARM]
  long armDone[NARM]                    ' the arm finished and its gate was decided
  long armPass[NARM]                    ' its gate passed
  long lastBaseOk
  long lastFirst
  long lastStray
  ' print buffers
  byte rowStr[NSLOT + 1]
  byte agreeStr[NSLOT + 1]
  ' every printed line is built here and sent by ONE debug() record (ln_out)
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos

PUB main() | status, pStack
'' Run the three arms in order; each prints its runs, its gate and its
'' verdicts when it completes; then the verdict summary.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local status - SUCCESS, or the failure that ended the run
' @local pStack - hub address of this method's locals: cog 0's stack

  pStack := @status
  linePos := 0
  ' the layout check runs before the first write to the fixed data area it protects
  if pStack + STACK_MARGIN > HUB_DATA_LO or HUB_DATA_END > HUB_TOP16K
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: hub layout - cog 0 stack at "))
    ln_h(pStack)
    ln_s(string(" must lie at least "))
    ln_h(STACK_MARGIN)
    ln_s(string(" below the data at "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_LO)
    ln_s(string(", and the data end "))
    ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
    ln_s(string(" must lie below "))
    ln_h(HUB_TOP16K)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  if @runTabEnd - @runTab <> NRUN * RT_W or @chTabEnd - @chTab <> NCH * CT_W
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: run tables hold "))
    ln_d(@runTabEnd - @runTab)
    ln_s(string(" / "))
    ln_d(@chTabEnd - @chTab)
    ln_s(string(" bytes, expected "))
    ln_d(NRUN * RT_W)
    ln_s(string(" / "))
    ln_d(NCH * CT_W)
    ln_out()
    finish()
  reset_tallies()
  fill_regions()

  print_header(pStack)

  status := run_arm0()
  if status == SUCCESS
    run_arm_s()                         ' arm 1 first: the positive control for block release
    run_arm_q()

  print_summary()
  finish()

PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_d(value) | divisor, bStarted
' Append a signed decimal to the line.
'
' @param value - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  if value == NEGX
    ln_s(string("-2147483648"))
  else
    if value < 0
      ln_c("-")
      value := -value
    divisor := 1_000_000_000
    bStarted := FALSE
    repeat 10
      if value >= divisor or bStarted or divisor == 1
        ln_c("0" + value / divisor)
        value //= divisor
        bStarted := TRUE
      divisor /= 10

PRI ln_hx(value, digits) | idx, nibble
' Append "$" and the low digits hex digits of value.
'
' @param value - the number
' @param digits - hex digits to print (1..8)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, digits-1 .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from digits - 1 to 0
    nibble := (value >> (idx * 4)) & $F
    if nibble < 10
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - 10)

PRI ln_h(value) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param value - the long

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from 7 to 0
    nibble := (value >> (idx * 4)) & $F
    if nibble < 10
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - 10)
    if idx == 4
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_row8(pLongs) | idx
' Append 8 longs as decimals separated by single spaces.
'
' @param pLongs - hub address of the first long

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index 0..7

  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if idx > 0
      ln_c(" ")
    ln_d(long[pLongs][idx])

PRI ln_hex8(pLongs) | idx
' Append 8 longs in hex, each preceded by a space.
'
' @param pLongs - hub address of the first long

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index 0..7

  repeat idx from 0 to BLKN - 1
    ln_c(" ")
    ln_h(long[pLongs][idx])

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' set-up, the run tables and the command channel
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_header(pStack)
' Print the rig identity, the layout and every prediction before the run.
'
' @param pStack - hub address of main()'s locals (cog 0's stack)

  say(string("=== P2 Errata O29C: E8's workaround for a SETQ block RDLONG after a no-wait RDFAST, and one released block read at k=0 (pnut-ts v1.55.8 -d, clk 200 MHz) ==="))
  say(string("values: primer $A5A5_0001; sentinel $5A5A_0002; seed $C3C3_0003; block long i $5A5A_0100+i; stream long n $1E1E_0000+n; cog guard long i $6D6D_0000+i; unwritten $EEEE_EEEE"))
  ln_s(string("hub: stream "))
  ln_h(HUB_STRM)
  ln_s(string(" table "))
  ln_h(HUB_TBL)
  ln_s(string(" block "))
  ln_h(HUB_BLK)
  ln_s(string(" primer "))
  ln_h(HUB_PRIM)
  ln_s(string(" records "))
  ln_h(HUB_RES)
  ln_s(string(" cog copies "))
  ln_h(HUB_DUMP)
  ln_c("/")
  ln_h(HUB_DUMP0)
  ln_s(string("; data end "))
  ln_h(HUB_DATA_END)
  ln_s(string("; measuring-cog image "))
  ln_h(@pasm)
  ln_s(string("; last VAR byte array "))
  ln_h(@lineBuf)
  ln_s(string("; cog 0 stack "))
  ln_h(pStack)
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("measuring cog: image $000-"))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@pasm_end) - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string("; loop variables "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_cmd), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_tmp), 3)
  ln_s(string("; guard bands "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_lo), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_lo) + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string(" and "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_hi), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_guard_hi) + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string("; sacrificial range "))
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_blk0), 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(cog_addr(@c_blk0) + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_out()
  say(string("codes: image R  P primer  S sentinel  D seed  F stream long  U unwritten  X other | block  . right block  P primer in some longs  D seed in some longs  M both  U unwritten  X other"))
  say(string("agree: . all 16 identical, else hex count identical to rep 0. delta = (ar - af) mod 8. Every run: 16 repetitions x 64 cells"))
  say(string("ORDER: arm 0, then arm 1 (characterisation at k=0: the positive control for block release), then arm 2 (the E8 workaround runs)"))
  say(string("FRESH COG: every trial of arm 1 and every run of arm 2 runs in a fresh measuring cog - COGINIT, start-up handshake, cog-RAM baseline, the run, then COGSTOP; a cog that does not finish within 1 s is stopped and loses only its run"))
  say(string("ARM 0 MUST (EF-084): C1 sentinel 1024; PS stream long 1024; T1 k=0 43 primer per repetition by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 (688 of 1024); T1 k=7 sentinel 1024. Else RIG FAIL: no later verdict counts"))
  say(string("ARM 1 RECORDS (no prediction): single block trials at k=0, each in a fresh cog, then a ping (100 ms); per cell 1 NOP control (MUST right block, completed, answered, cog RAM intact) and 4 no-wait RDFAST trials;"))
  say(string("  cells (EF-084 map): af0/ar0 and af2/ar0 released (P), af0/ar4 and af1/ar3 escaping (S); recorded: block per long, completed, answered, changed registers, block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range"))
  say(string("  RELEASE SHOWN = a released-cell trial with the primer in long 0, a long left unwritten (seed or fill), or a cog that did not finish within 1 s (stopped)"))
  say(string("ARM 2 clocks, start of the RDFAST to start of the block RDLONG: QB T k6 16 (rdfast 2 + 6 nop 12 + setq 2: E8's rule exactly, 7 non-hub instructions); QB T k7 18; QB T k8 20; QB C k0 the waiting RDFAST's own wait + 2"))
  say(string("ARM 2 MUST: QB N k0 the right block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024 records, 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range, no block or primer long outside it, the cog completes the run; else the arm's gate fails"))
  say(string("ARM 2 PREDICT for QB C k0, QB T k6, QB T k7, QB T k8: (a) the right block in all 1024 records; (b) 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range, no block or primer long outside it; (c) the cog completes the run"))
  say(string("  CONFIRMED if (a), (b), (c) all hold AND arm 1 showed a release with its gate passed, else INCONCLUSIVE (a clean run proves nothing without it); REFUTED naming each part that failed: wrong long / register change / did not finish within 1 s (stopped)"))
  say(string("rig fails: arm 0 not reproduced; a NOP control not clean; a baseline cog-RAM copy not equal to the loaded image; a mode echo mismatch"))

PRI fill_regions() | idx
' Write every fixed data region its pattern.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    long[HUB_STRM][idx] := STRM_V + idx
  longfill(HUB_TBL, SENTV, NSLOT)
  repeat idx from 0 to BLK_LONGS - 1
    long[HUB_BLK][idx] := BLK_V + idx
  long[HUB_PRIM] := PRIMV

PRI region_damage() : damageCnt | idx
' Count read-only data longs that no longer hold their pattern.
'
' @returns damageCnt - changed longs (stream, table, block source, primer)

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - long index inside a region

  damageCnt := 0
  repeat idx from 0 to STRM_LONGS - 1
    if long[HUB_STRM][idx] <> STRM_V + idx
      damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if long[HUB_TBL][idx] <> SENTV
      damageCnt++
  repeat idx from 0 to BLK_LONGS - 1
    if long[HUB_BLK][idx] <> BLK_V + idx
      damageCnt++
  if long[HUB_PRIM] <> PRIMV
    damageCnt++

PRI check_damage(armIdx) | damageCnt
' After a run or trial: count damaged read-only data, report it, re-fill.
'
' @param armIdx - the arm the run belongs to

' Local Variables:
' @local damageCnt - data longs changed

  damageCnt := region_damage()
  if damageCnt > 0
    armDamage[armIdx] += damageCnt
    ln_s(string("  REGION DAMAGE: "))
    ln_d(damageCnt)
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed (a stray hub write) - regions re-filled"))
    fill_regions()

PRI reset_tallies()
' Clear every tally.
'

  bytefill(@cellCode, 0, NRUN * NCELL)
  bytefill(@cellAgree, 0, NRUN * NCELL)
  longfill(@runCnt, 0, NRUN * NVC)
  longfill(@runRep0, 0, NRUN * NVC)
  longfill(@runDelta, 0, NRUN * NSLOT)
  longfill(@runDelta2, 0, NRUN * NSLOT)
  longfill(@runDisagree, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runGoodAll, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOther, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@runOtherVal, 0, NRUN)
  longfill(@blkPrim, 0, NBRUN * BLKN)
  longfill(@blkSeed, 0, NBRUN * BLKN)
  longfill(@blkOth, 0, NBRUN * BLKN)
  longfill(@blkOthVal, 0, NBRUN)
  longfill(@blkOthIdx, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@qState, ST_NOTRUN, NBRUN)
  longfill(@qBaseOk, FALSE, NBRUN)
  longfill(@intChanged, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@intFirst, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@intStray, -1, NBRUN)
  longfill(@chRec, UNWRITTEN, NCH * BLKN)
  longfill(@chSac, UNWRITTEN, NCH * BLKN)
  longfill(@chState, ST_NOTRUN, NCH)
  longfill(@chAns, FALSE, NCH)
  longfill(@chBaseOk, FALSE, NCH)
  longfill(@chChanged, -1, NCH)
  longfill(@chStray, -1, NCH)
  longfill(@armDamage, 0, NARM)
  longfill(@armDone, FALSE, NARM)
  longfill(@armPass, FALSE, NARM)
  lastBaseOk := FALSE
  lastFirst := -1
  lastStray := -1

PRI run_fld(runIdx, fieldIdx) : value
' @param runIdx - run index
' @param fieldIdx - RF_* field
' @returns value - the run table byte

  value := byte[@runTab][runIdx * RT_W + fieldIdx]

PRI ch_fld(trialIdx, fieldIdx) : value
' @param trialIdx - arm 1 trial index
' @param fieldIdx - CF_* field
' @returns value - the trial table byte

  value := byte[@chTab][trialIdx * CT_W + fieldIdx]

PRI cog_addr(hubAddr) : cogAddr
' @param hubAddr - hub address of a long in the measuring cog's image
' @returns cogAddr - its cog register address

  cogAddr := (hubAddr - @pasm) >> 2

PRI start_meas_cog() : status | startCt
' Start a measuring cog (COGINIT, cog execution) and wait for its start-up
' handshake.  On a failed handshake the cog is stopped.  Prints a line on
' failure only.
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS or E_NO_START

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT at the start of the start-up timeout

  status := SUCCESS
  mbox[MB_CMD] := 0                     ' a fresh cog must not see a stale command
  mbox[MB_ALIVE] := 0
  measCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @pasm, @mbox)
  if measCog < 0
    ln_s(string("  COG START FAILED: coginit expected a free cog (0..7), got "))
    ln_d(measCog)
    ln_out()
    status := E_NO_START
    return
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_ALIVE] == STAT_READY
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq
      ln_s(string("  COG START FAILED: cog "))
      ln_d(measCog)
      ln_s(string(" start-up handshake expected $0000_0A11 within 1 s, got "))
      ln_h(mbox[MB_ALIVE])
      say(string("; the cog was stopped (COGSTOP)"))
      cogstop(measCog)
      status := E_NO_START
      return

PRI fresh_cog() : status | addr, imgLen, varLo, varHi, matchCnt, checkCnt
' Start a fresh measuring cog and take its cog-RAM baseline (CMD_SNAP),
' checked against the loaded image outside the loop variables.  Sets
' lastBaseOk.  On a baseline timeout the cog is left running: the caller
' stops it.
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS / E_NO_START / E_RIG_FAIL / E_MODE_FAIL

' Local Variables:
' @local addr - cog register address
' @local imgLen - registers in the loaded image
' @local varLo - first loop-variable register
' @local varHi - last loop-variable register
' @local matchCnt - image registers equal in the copy
' @local checkCnt - image registers compared

  lastBaseOk := FALSE
  status := start_meas_cog()
  if status <> SUCCESS
    return
  longfill(HUB_DUMP, UNWRITTEN, COG_DUMP_N)
  status := send_cmd(CMD_SNAP, 0, FIFO_WAIT, 0, 0, HUB_BLK, RUN_TIMEOUT_MS)
  if status == E_RIG_FAIL
    ln_s(string("  BASELINE FAILED: fresh cog "))
    ln_d(measCog)
    say(string(" did not answer its baseline command within 1 s"))
  if status <> SUCCESS
    return
  longmove(HUB_DUMP0, HUB_DUMP, COG_DUMP_N)
  imgLen := cog_addr(@pasm_end)
  varLo := cog_addr(@c_cmd)
  varHi := cog_addr(@c_tmp)
  matchCnt := 0
  checkCnt := 0
  repeat addr from 0 to imgLen - 1
    if addr < varLo or addr > varHi
      checkCnt++
      if long[HUB_DUMP0][addr] == long[@pasm][addr]
        matchCnt++
  lastBaseOk := matchCnt == checkCnt
  ln_s(string("  fresh measuring cog "))
  ln_d(measCog)
  ln_s(string(" (COGINIT); its baseline cog-RAM copy equals the loaded image in "))
  ln_d(matchCnt)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(checkCnt)
  say(string(" image registers outside the loop variables (MUST be all)"))

PRI send_run(runIdx, timeoutMs) : status | cmdId, pTbl, modeVal
' Build the command for one run from the run table and send it.
'
' @param runIdx - run index
' @param timeoutMs - milliseconds to wait for the measuring cog
' @returns status - SUCCESS / E_RIG_FAIL / E_MODE_FAIL

' Local Variables:
' @local cmdId - CMD_*
' @local pTbl - table / block base
' @local modeVal - FIFO D value

  if run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_B
    cmdId := CMD_B
    pTbl := HUB_BLK
  else
    cmdId := CMD_R
    pTbl := HUB_TBL
  if run_fld(runIdx, RF_NOWAIT)
    modeVal := FIFO_NO_WAIT
  else
    modeVal := FIFO_WAIT
  status := send_cmd(cmdId, run_fld(runIdx, RF_COPY), modeVal, 0, 0, pTbl, timeoutMs)

PRI send_cmd(cmdId, copyIdx, modeVal, afVal, arVal, pTbl, timeoutMs) : status | startCt
' Hand one command to the measuring cog and wait for it to clear MB_CMD.
'
' @param cmdId - CMD_*
' @param copyIdx - trial copy (CP_*)
' @param modeVal - the RDFAST D value under test
' @param afVal - CMD_B1: the stream slot bits
' @param arVal - CMD_B1: the block's slot bits
' @param pTbl - table / block base
' @param timeoutMs - milliseconds to wait
' @returns status - SUCCESS; E_RIG_FAIL on a timeout; E_MODE_FAIL (after
'   printing its line) when the mode echoed back is not the mode sent

' Local Variables:
' @local startCt - CT when the command was issued

  status := SUCCESS
  mbox[MB_COPY] := copyIdx
  mbox[MB_MODE] := modeVal
  mbox[MB_AF] := afVal
  mbox[MB_AR] := arVal
  mbox[MB_PRIM] := HUB_PRIM
  mbox[MB_TBL] := pTbl
  mbox[MB_ECHO] := UNWRITTEN
  mbox[MB_CMD] := cmdId
  startCt := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_CMD] == 0
    if getct() - startCt > clkfreq / 1000 * timeoutMs
      status := E_RIG_FAIL
      quit
  if status == SUCCESS and mbox[MB_ECHO] <> modeVal
    ln_s(string("  MODE ECHO FAIL: command "))
    ln_d(cmdId)
    ln_s(string(" copy "))
    ln_d(copyIdx)
    ln_s(string(" ran with FIFO D "))
    ln_h(mbox[MB_ECHO])
    ln_s(string(", expected "))
    ln_h(modeVal)
    say(string(" (harness)"))
    status := E_MODE_FAIL

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' the arms
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI run_arm0() : status | runIdx
' Arm 0 on one measuring cog: C1, PS, T1 k=0, T1 k=7; then its gate.
'
' @returns status - SUCCESS, or the harness failure that ends the run

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run index

  say(string("===== ARM 0: POSITIVE CONTROL (C1, PS, T1 k=0, T1 k=7 - the O29 construction; MUST reproduce EF-084, else RIG FAIL and no later verdict counts) ====="))
  status := start_meas_cog()
  if status <> SUCCESS
    say(string("RIG FAIL: arm 0's measuring cog did not start (line above); the run ends here"))
    return
  ln_s(string("measuring cog "))
  ln_d(measCog)
  say(string(" running (arm 0)"))
  repeat runIdx from RUN_C1 to RUN_T1F
    print_run_header(runIdx)
    longfill(HUB_RES, UNWRITTEN, NTRIAL)
    status := send_run(runIdx, RUN_TIMEOUT_MS)
    if status == E_RIG_FAIL
      cogstop(measCog)
      ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not finish run "))
      ln_runname(runIdx)
      say(string(" within 1 s (done flag never cleared); it was stopped (COGSTOP) and the run ends here"))
      return
    process_run(runIdx)
    print_run(runIdx)
    check_damage(ARM_P)
    if status <> SUCCESS
      cogstop(measCog)
      say(string("RIG FAIL: mode echo in arm 0 (line above); the measuring cog was stopped (COGSTOP) and the run ends here"))
      return
  cogstop(measCog)
  say(string("  arm 0's measuring cog stopped (COGSTOP); every later run and trial starts a fresh one"))
  armPass[ARM_P] := arm0_gate()
  armDone[ARM_P] := TRUE
  print_rig_line()

PRI run_arm_q() | runIdx, bIdx, status
' Arm 2: every run in a fresh measuring cog; then its gate and verdicts.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run index
' @local bIdx - arm 2 slot (QS_*)
' @local status - command result

  say(string("===== ARM 2: SETQ BLOCK RDLONG, E8 WORKAROUND (QB N k0, QB C k0, QB T k6, QB T k7, QB T k8; each run in a fresh measuring cog; cog-RAM integrity checked after every run) ====="))
  repeat runIdx from RUN_Q to NRUN - 1
    bIdx := runIdx - RUN_Q
    print_run_header(runIdx)
    status := fresh_cog()
    if status == E_NO_START
      qState[bIdx] := ST_NOSTART
      ln_s(string("  NOT RUN: "))
      ln_runname(runIdx)
      say(string(" - a fresh measuring cog did not start (line above); the next run starts another"))
      next
    qBaseOk[bIdx] := lastBaseOk
    if status <> SUCCESS
      cogstop(measCog)
      if status == E_MODE_FAIL
        qState[bIdx] := ST_ECHO
      else
        qState[bIdx] := ST_NOBASE
      ln_s(string("  NOT RUN: "))
      ln_runname(runIdx)
      say(string(" - the fresh cog's baseline command failed (line above); the cog was stopped (COGSTOP)"))
      next
    longfill(HUB_RES, UNWRITTEN, NREC_B)
    longfill(HUB_DUMP, UNWRITTEN, COG_DUMP_N)
    status := send_run(runIdx, RUN_TIMEOUT_MS)
    cogstop(measCog)
    if status == E_RIG_FAIL
      qState[bIdx] := ST_LOST
      ln_s(string("  OBSERVED: run "))
      ln_runname(runIdx)
      say(string(" did not finish within 1 s (stopped by COGSTOP); the records it wrote follow (U = never written); the next run starts a fresh cog"))
    elseif status == E_MODE_FAIL
      qState[bIdx] := ST_ECHO
    else
      qState[bIdx] := ST_DONE
    process_run(runIdx)
    print_run(runIdx)
    intChanged[bIdx] := integrity_check(FALSE, runIdx)
    intFirst[bIdx] := lastFirst
    intStray[bIdx] := lastStray
    check_damage(ARM_Q)
  armPass[ARM_Q] := q_gate()
  armDone[ARM_Q] := TRUE
  verdict_q(QS_C)
  verdict_q(QS_T6)
  verdict_q(QS_T7)
  verdict_q(QS_T8)

PRI run_arm_s() | trialIdx
' Arm 1: single trials, each in a fresh measuring cog; then its gate and
' its OBSERVED lines.  Runs before arm 2: its positive control for release.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local trialIdx - arm 1 trial index

  say(string("===== ARM 1: CHARACTERISATION AT k=0 (RECORDS; the positive control for block release, run before arm 2; single block trials, each in a fresh measuring cog, then a ping within 100 ms) ====="))
  repeat trialIdx from 0 to NCH - 1
    run_trial(trialIdx)
  armPass[ARM_S] := s_gate()
  armDone[ARM_S] := TRUE
  observed_s()

PRI run_trial(trialIdx) | kind, afIdx, arIdx, copyIdx, modeVal, status
' One arm 1 trial: fresh cog, baseline, the trial, the ping, COGSTOP; print it.
'
' @param trialIdx - arm 1 trial index

' Local Variables:
' @local kind - KD_NOP (control) or KD_TEST
' @local afIdx - stream slot bits
' @local arIdx - block slot bits
' @local copyIdx - trial copy
' @local modeVal - FIFO D value
' @local status - command result

  kind := ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND)
  afIdx := ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AF)
  arIdx := ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AR)
  if kind == KD_NOP
    copyIdx := CP_B_NOP
    modeVal := FIFO_WAIT
  else
    copyIdx := CP_B_RF0
    modeVal := FIFO_NO_WAIT
  ln_s(string("TRIAL "))
  ln_trialname(trialIdx)
  if kind == KD_NOP
    ln_s(string(" (NOP CONTROL): rdlong primer $A5A5_0001 / NOP in place of the RDFAST"))
  else
    ln_s(string(" (TEST): rdlong primer $A5A5_0001 / rdfast D=$8000_0000"))
  ln_s(string(" / 0 NOP / setq #7 / rdlong block of 8 longs; EF-084 map: "))
  if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_REL)
    ln_s(string("released (P)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("escaping (S)"))
  ln_s(string("; T1 k=0 in this run "))
  if cellCode[RUN_T1 * NCELL + afIdx * NSLOT + arIdx] == VC_PRIM
    ln_s(string("released this cell"))
  else
    ln_s(string("did not release this cell"))
  say(string("; then a ping (100 ms)"))
  status := fresh_cog()
  if status == E_NO_START
    chState[trialIdx] := ST_NOSTART
    ln_s(string("  NOT RUN: "))
    ln_trialname(trialIdx)
    say(string(" - a fresh measuring cog did not start (line above)"))
    return
  chBaseOk[trialIdx] := lastBaseOk
  if status <> SUCCESS
    cogstop(measCog)
    if status == E_MODE_FAIL
      chState[trialIdx] := ST_ECHO
    else
      chState[trialIdx] := ST_NOBASE
    ln_s(string("  NOT RUN: "))
    ln_trialname(trialIdx)
    say(string(" - the fresh cog's baseline command failed (line above); the cog was stopped (COGSTOP)"))
    return
  longfill(HUB_RES, UNWRITTEN, BLKN)
  longfill(HUB_DUMP, UNWRITTEN, COG_DUMP_N)
  status := send_cmd(CMD_B1, copyIdx, modeVal, afIdx, arIdx, HUB_BLK, RUN_TIMEOUT_MS)
  longmove(@chRec[trialIdx * BLKN], HUB_RES, BLKN)
  if status == E_RIG_FAIL
    chState[trialIdx] := ST_LOST
  elseif status == E_MODE_FAIL
    chState[trialIdx] := ST_ECHO
  else
    chState[trialIdx] := ST_DONE
  if chState[trialIdx] <> ST_LOST
    mbox[MB_ALIVE] := 0
    status := send_cmd(CMD_PING, copyIdx, modeVal, afIdx, arIdx, HUB_BLK, PING_TIMEOUT_MS)
    chAns[trialIdx] := status <> E_RIG_FAIL and mbox[MB_ALIVE] == STAT_PONG
    if status == E_MODE_FAIL
      chState[trialIdx] := ST_ECHO
  cogstop(measCog)
  if chAns[trialIdx]
    longmove(@chSac[trialIdx * BLKN], HUB_DUMP + cog_addr(@c_blk0) * 4, BLKN)
    chChanged[trialIdx] := integrity_check(TRUE, trialIdx)
    chStray[trialIdx] := lastStray
  print_trial(trialIdx)
  check_damage(ARM_S)

PRI integrity_check(bTrial, idx) : changed | addr, sacLo, varLo, varHi, tmpAddr, checkCnt, datum
' Compare the cog-RAM copy with the same cog's baseline: list and count every
' changed register outside the sacrificial range and the loop variables;
' list and count every changed register outside the sacrificial range that
' now holds a block-source long or the primer (the primer in c_tmp, its own
' destination, excepted).  Sets lastFirst and lastStray.
'
' @param bTrial - FALSE: arm 2 run; TRUE: arm 1 trial
' @param idx - the run or trial index
' @returns changed - changed registers, or -1 when no copy arrived

' Local Variables:
' @local addr - cog register address
' @local sacLo - first sacrificial register
' @local varLo - first loop-variable register
' @local varHi - last loop-variable register
' @local tmpAddr - c_tmp (the primer read's destination)
' @local checkCnt - registers compared for "changed"
' @local datum - the register's value in the copy

  lastFirst := -1
  if long[HUB_DUMP][0] == UNWRITTEN and long[HUB_DUMP][COG_DUMP_N - 1] == UNWRITTEN
    changed := -1
    lastStray := -1
    ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
    ln_label(bTrial, idx)
    say(string(": no cog-RAM copy arrived (the copy area still holds $EEEE_EEEE)"))
    return
  sacLo := cog_addr(@c_blk0)
  varLo := cog_addr(@c_cmd)
  varHi := cog_addr(@c_tmp)
  tmpAddr := cog_addr(@c_tmp)
  changed := 0
  lastStray := 0
  checkCnt := 0
  repeat addr from 0 to COG_DUMP_N - 1
    if addr < sacLo or addr > sacLo + BLKN - 1
      datum := long[HUB_DUMP][addr]
      if addr < varLo or addr > varHi
        checkCnt++
        if datum <> long[HUB_DUMP0][addr]
          changed++
          if changed == 1
            lastFirst := addr
          if changed <= INT_SHOW
            ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
            ln_label(bTrial, idx)
            ln_s(string(": cog register "))
            ln_hx(addr, 3)
            ln_s(string(" changed: baseline "))
            ln_h(long[HUB_DUMP0][addr])
            ln_s(string(" now "))
            ln_h(datum)
            ln_out()
      if datum <> long[HUB_DUMP0][addr] and ((datum - BLK_V) +< BLK_LONGS or (datum == PRIMV and addr <> tmpAddr))
        lastStray++
        if lastStray <= INT_SHOW
          ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
          ln_label(bTrial, idx)
          ln_s(string(": block/primer long "))
          ln_h(datum)
          ln_s(string(" in cog register "))
          ln_hx(addr, 3)
          ln_s(string(" (baseline "))
          ln_h(long[HUB_DUMP0][addr])
          say(string(")"))
  ln_s(string("  INTEGRITY "))
  ln_label(bTrial, idx)
  ln_s(string(": "))
  ln_d(changed)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(checkCnt)
  ln_s(string(" cog registers outside the sacrificial range "))
  ln_hx(sacLo, 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(sacLo + BLKN - 1, 3)
  ln_s(string(" and the loop variables "))
  ln_hx(varLo, 3)
  ln_c("-")
  ln_hx(varHi, 3)
  ln_s(string(" changed since the baseline; block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range: "))
  ln_d(lastStray)
  ln_out()

PRI ln_label(bTrial, idx)
' @param bTrial - FALSE: arm 2 run; TRUE: arm 1 trial
' @param idx - the run or trial index

  if bTrial
    ln_trialname(idx)
  else
    ln_runname(idx)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' classification
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI class_v(datum) : cls
' Image R classification.
'
' @param datum - a record long
' @returns cls - VC_*

  if datum == PRIMV
    cls := VC_PRIM
  elseif datum == SENTV
    cls := VC_SENT
  elseif datum == SEEDV
    cls := VC_SEED
  elseif datum == UNWRITTEN
    cls := VC_UNWR
  elseif (datum - STRM_V) +< STRM_LONGS
    cls := VC_STRM
  else
    cls := VC_OTHER

PRI vcchar(cls) : codeChar
' @param cls - VC_*
' @returns codeChar - P S D F U X

  codeChar := lookupz(cls: "P", "S", "D", "F", "U", "X")

PRI bcchar(cls) : codeChar
' @param cls - BC_* (U X in the shared slots)
' @returns codeChar - . P D M U X

  codeChar := lookupz(cls: ".", "P", "D", "M", "U", "X")

PRI agreechar(agreeCnt) : codeChar
' @param agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0 (1..16)
' @returns codeChar - "." for all 16, else the hex digit

  if agreeCnt == REPS
    codeChar := "."
  elseif agreeCnt < 10
    codeChar := "0" + agreeCnt
  else
    codeChar := "A" + agreeCnt - 10

PRI cell_delta(cellIdx) : deltaIdx
' @param cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @returns deltaIdx - (ar - af) mod 8

  deltaIdx := ((cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1)) - (cellIdx >> 3)) & (NSLOT - 1)

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' processing one run
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI process_run(runIdx)
' @param runIdx - run index

  if run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_PS
    process_ps(runIdx)
  elseif run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE) == SH_R
    process_r(runIdx)
  else
    process_b(runIdx)

PRI process_r(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, datum, cls, agreeCnt
' Classify an image R run: repetition-0 codes, agreement, totals, delta split.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's record
' @local datum - a record
' @local cls - its class
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][cellIdx]
    cls := class_v(firstVal)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
    if cls == VC_PRIM
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if cls <> VC_SENT
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      datum := long[HUB_RES][repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]
      cls := class_v(datum)
      runCnt[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
      if cls == VC_OTHER
        if runOther[runIdx] == 0
          runOtherVal[runIdx] := datum
        runOther[runIdx]++
      if cls == VC_SENT
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if datum == firstVal
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI process_ps(runIdx) | cellIdx, repIdx, firstVal, datum, agreeCnt, expVal
' Classify the PS run: every record must be the stream's first long, STRM_V + af.
' Cell code 1 = right, 0 = wrong.
'
' @param runIdx - RUN_PS

' Local Variables:
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local firstVal - repetition 0's record
' @local datum - a record
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0
' @local expVal - the stream's first long for this af

  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    expVal := STRM_V + (cellIdx >> 3)
    firstVal := long[HUB_RES][cellIdx]
    if firstVal == expVal
      cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := 1
    else
      cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := 0
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      datum := long[HUB_RES][repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx]
      if datum == expVal
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      elseif runOtherVal[runIdx] == 0
        runOtherVal[runIdx] := datum
      if datum == UNWRITTEN
        runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_UNWR]++
      if datum == firstVal
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI class_blk(pRec, arIdx, bIdx, bTally) : cls | j, datum, nPrim, nSeed, nOth, nUnwr
' Classify one 8-long block record against the block expected for ar.
'
' @param pRec - hub address of the record
' @param arIdx - the block's first slot bits (its first long is block long ar)
' @param bIdx - arm 2 slot
' @param bTally - TRUE: count per long index
' @returns cls - BC_*

' Local Variables:
' @local j - long index in the record
' @local datum - the long
' @local nPrim - longs holding the primer
' @local nSeed - longs holding the seed
' @local nOth - longs holding anything else
' @local nUnwr - longs holding the record-area fill

  nPrim := 0
  nSeed := 0
  nOth := 0
  nUnwr := 0
  repeat j from 0 to BLKN - 1
    datum := long[pRec][j]
    if datum == BLK_V + arIdx + j
      next
    if datum == PRIMV
      nPrim++
      if bTally
        blkPrim[bIdx * BLKN + j]++
    elseif datum == SEEDV
      nSeed++
      if bTally
        blkSeed[bIdx * BLKN + j]++
    elseif datum == UNWRITTEN
      nUnwr++
    else
      nOth++
      if bTally
        blkOth[bIdx * BLKN + j]++
        if blkOthIdx[bIdx] == -1
          blkOthIdx[bIdx] := j
          blkOthVal[bIdx] := datum
  if nUnwr > 0
    cls := BC_UNWR
  elseif nOth > 0
    cls := BC_OTHER
  elseif nPrim > 0 and nSeed > 0
    cls := BC_MIX
  elseif nPrim > 0
    cls := BC_PRIM
  elseif nSeed > 0
    cls := BC_SEED
  else
    cls := BC_OK

PRI same_block(pRecA, pRecB) : bSame | j
' @param pRecA - a record
' @param pRecB - another record
' @returns bSame - TRUE when all 8 longs are equal

' Local Variables:
' @local j - long index

  bSame := TRUE
  repeat j from 0 to BLKN - 1
    if long[pRecA][j] <> long[pRecB][j]
      bSame := FALSE

PRI process_b(runIdx) | bIdx, cellIdx, repIdx, pRec0, pRec, cls, agreeCnt
' Classify an arm 2 run: per-record classes, per-long counts, agreement.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local bIdx - arm 2 slot
' @local cellIdx - af * 8 + ar
' @local repIdx - repetition
' @local pRec0 - repetition 0's record
' @local pRec - a record
' @local cls - BC_*
' @local agreeCnt - repetitions identical to repetition 0

  bIdx := runIdx - RUN_Q
  repeat cellIdx from 0 to NCELL - 1
    pRec0 := HUB_RES + cellIdx * BLKN * 4
    cls := class_blk(pRec0, cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1), bIdx, FALSE)
    cellCode[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := cls
    runRep0[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
    if cls == BC_PRIM or cls == BC_MIX
      runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    if cls <> BC_OK
      runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT + cell_delta(cellIdx)]++
    agreeCnt := 0
    repeat repIdx from 0 to REPS - 1
      pRec := HUB_RES + (repIdx * NCELL + cellIdx) * BLKN * 4
      cls := class_blk(pRec, cellIdx & (NSLOT - 1), bIdx, TRUE)
      runCnt[runIdx * NVC + cls]++
      if cls == BC_OTHER
        runOther[runIdx]++
      if cls == BC_OK
        runGoodAll[runIdx]++
      if same_block(pRec, pRec0)
        agreeCnt++
    cellAgree[runIdx * NCELL + cellIdx] := agreeCnt
    if agreeCnt <> REPS
      runDisagree[runIdx]++

PRI ch_pattern(trialIdx) : pat | j, arIdx
' Arm 1: the block pattern recorded right after a trial.
'
' @param trialIdx - arm 1 trial index
' @returns pat - PAT_OK right block / PAT_P1 long 0 the primer, longs 1-7
'   still the seed / PAT_OTH other

' Local Variables:
' @local j - long index
' @local arIdx - the block's slot bits

  arIdx := ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AR)
  pat := PAT_OK
  repeat j from 0 to BLKN - 1
    if chRec[trialIdx * BLKN + j] <> BLK_V + arIdx + j
      pat := PAT_OTH
  if pat == PAT_OTH and chRec[trialIdx * BLKN] == PRIMV
    pat := PAT_P1
    repeat j from 1 to BLKN - 1
      if chRec[trialIdx * BLKN + j] <> SEEDV
        pat := PAT_OTH

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' printing
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_runname(runIdx)
' Append the run's printable name, e.g. "T1 k0", "QB T k7".
'
' @param runIdx - run index

  if run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM) == ARM_P
    ln_s(lookupz(runIdx: string("C1"), string("PS"), string("T1"), string("T1")))
  else
    ln_s(string("QB "))
    ln_c(lookupz(run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND): "N", "?", "C", "T"))
  ln_s(string(" k"))
  ln_d(run_fld(runIdx, RF_K))

PRI ln_trialname(trialIdx) | n, u
' Append an arm 1 trial's printable name, e.g. "QS T k0 af0 ar4 #2".
'
' @param trialIdx - arm 1 trial index

' Local Variables:
' @local n - the trial's number among the trials with its kind, af and ar
' @local u - an earlier trial index

  ln_s(string("QS "))
  if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND) == KD_NOP
    ln_c("N")
  else
    ln_c("T")
  ln_s(string(" k0 af"))
  ln_d(ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AF))
  ln_s(string(" ar"))
  ln_d(ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AR))
  n := 1
  if trialIdx > 0
    repeat u from 0 to trialIdx - 1
      if ch_fld(u, CF_KIND) == ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND) and ch_fld(u, CF_AF) == ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AF) and ch_fld(u, CF_AR) == ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AR)
        n++
  ln_s(string(" #"))
  ln_d(n)

PRI print_run_header(runIdx) | shape, kind, kVal
' Print the run's sequence, and its MUST / PREDICT line, before its rows.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local kVal - NOPs between the RDFAST and the test instruction

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
  kVal := run_fld(runIdx, RF_K)
  ln_s(string("RUN "))
  ln_runname(runIdx)
  ln_s(string(" ("))
  ln_s(lookupz(kind: string("NOP CONTROL"), string("POSITIVE CONTROL"), string("WAITING FORM"), string("TEST")))
  ln_s(string("): rdlong primer $A5A5_0001 / "))
  if shape == SH_PS
    ln_s(string("rdfast D=$8000_0000 / waitx #200 / rflong"))
  else
    if kind == KD_NOP
      ln_s(string("NOP in place of the RDFAST"))
    else
      ln_s(string("rdfast D="))
      if run_fld(runIdx, RF_NOWAIT)
        ln_h(FIFO_NO_WAIT)
      else
        ln_h(FIFO_WAIT)
    ln_s(string(" / "))
    ln_d(kVal)
    ln_s(string(" NOP / "))
    if shape == SH_B
      ln_s(string("setq #7 / rdlong block of 8 longs into the sacrificial registers"))
    else
      ln_s(string("rdlong test"))
    if kind <> KD_NOP
      ln_s(string("; start of the RDFAST to start of the "))
      if shape == SH_B
        ln_s(string("block RDLONG: "))
      else
        ln_s(string("RDLONG: "))
      if not run_fld(runIdx, RF_NOWAIT)
        ln_s(string("the waiting RDFAST's own wait + 2 clocks"))
      else
        if shape == SH_B
          ln_d(2 + kVal * 2 + 2)
        else
          ln_d(2 + kVal * 2)
        ln_s(string(" clocks"))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("    "))
  ln_expect(runIdx)
  ln_out()

PRI ln_expect(runIdx) | shape, kind
' Append the run's MUST / PREDICT statement.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local kind - KD_*

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
  if kind == KD_PS
    ln_s(string("MUST: the stream's first long $1E1E_0000+af in all 1024 records, else RIG FAIL (the RDFAST under test would not be starting a stream)"))
  elseif kind == KD_NOP
    if shape == SH_B
      ln_s(string("MUST: the block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024 records, 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range, no block or primer long outside it, the cog completes the run; else the arm's gate fails"))
    else
      ln_s(string("MUST: sentinel $5A5A_0002 in all 1024 records, else RIG FAIL"))
  elseif run_fld(runIdx, RF_ARM) == ARM_P
    if run_fld(runIdx, RF_K) == 0
      ln_s(string("MUST (EF-084): 43 primer per repetition, by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2; every other record sentinel"))
    else
      ln_s(string("MUST (EF-084): sentinel in all 1024 records"))
  else
    ln_s(string("PREDICT: (a) the right block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024 records, (b) 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range and no block or primer long outside it, (c) the cog completes the run;"))
    ln_s(string(" CONFIRMED if all hold and arm 1 showed a release (else INCONCLUSIVE); REFUTED naming each part that failed: wrong long / register change / did not finish within 1 s (stopped)"))

PRI print_run(runIdx) | afIdx, arIdx, cellIdx, shape
' Print a run's raw rows (repetition 0 per af, agreement) and its totals.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local afIdx - stream slot bits
' @local arIdx - test-address slot bits
' @local cellIdx - index into the per-cell arrays
' @local shape - SH_*

  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  repeat afIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    repeat arIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
      cellIdx := runIdx * NCELL + afIdx * NSLOT + arIdx
      agreeStr[arIdx] := agreechar(cellAgree[cellIdx])
      if shape == SH_PS
        rowStr[arIdx] := lookupz(cellCode[cellIdx]: "X", ".")
      elseif shape == SH_R
        rowStr[arIdx] := vcchar(cellCode[cellIdx])
      else
        rowStr[arIdx] := bcchar(cellCode[cellIdx])
    agreeStr[NSLOT] := 0
    rowStr[NSLOT] := 0
    ln_s(string("  "))
    ln_runname(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" af"))
    ln_d(afIdx)
    ln_s(string(" rep0 a0-7: "))
    ln_s(@rowStr)
    ln_s(string("  agree "))
    say(@agreeStr)
  print_totals(runIdx)

PRI ln_lead(runIdx)
' Append "  <run name>", the lead of every per-run total line.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_runname(runIdx)

PRI print_totals(runIdx) | base, shape, bIdx
' Print a run's totals: classes over all repetitions, repetition-0 delta splits.
'
' @param runIdx - run index

' Local Variables:
' @local base - index of the run's first class count
' @local shape - SH_*
' @local bIdx - arm 2 slot

  base := runIdx * NVC
  shape := run_fld(runIdx, RF_SHAPE)
  if shape == SH_PS
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: stream's first long right in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 records (. right, X wrong); first wrong value "))
    ln_h(runOtherVal[runIdx])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
  elseif shape == SH_R
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps: primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" sentinel "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SENT])
    ln_s(string(" seed "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" stream "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_STRM])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | rep0 primer "))
    ln_d(runRep0[base + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | rep0 not sentinel by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    if runOther[runIdx] > 0
      ln_lead(runIdx)
      ln_s(string(" first other value "))
      ln_h(runOtherVal[runIdx])
      ln_s(string(" ("))
      ln_d(runOther[runIdx])
      say(string(" other values in the run)"))
  else
    bIdx := runIdx - RUN_Q
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" all reps (records of 8 longs): right block "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_OK])
    ln_s(string(" primer-in-record "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" seed-in-record "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_SEED])
    ln_s(string(" both "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_MIX])
    ln_s(string(" other "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_OTHER])
    ln_s(string(" unwritten "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + BC_UNWR])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 | rep0 records with the primer by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | rep0 not the right block by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta2[runIdx * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" | cells with disagreeing reps "))
    ln_d(runDisagree[runIdx])
    ln_out()
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" per long 0-7, all reps: primer "))
    ln_row8(@blkPrim[bIdx * BLKN])
    ln_s(string(" | seed "))
    ln_row8(@blkSeed[bIdx * BLKN])
    ln_s(string(" | other "))
    ln_row8(@blkOth[bIdx * BLKN])
    if blkOthIdx[bIdx] <> -1
      ln_s(string(" | first other value "))
      ln_h(blkOthVal[bIdx])
      ln_s(string(" in long "))
      ln_d(blkOthIdx[bIdx])
    ln_out()
  if runCnt[base + VC_UNWR] > 0
    ln_lead(runIdx)
    ln_s(string(" never written (U, $EEEE_EEEE): "))
    ln_d(runCnt[base + VC_UNWR])
    say(string(" records"))

PRI print_trial(trialIdx) | st, pat
' Print one arm 1 trial: its block, completion, ping and cog-RAM result.
'
' @param trialIdx - arm 1 trial index

' Local Variables:
' @local st - ST_*
' @local pat - PAT_*

  st := chState[trialIdx]
  pat := ch_pattern(trialIdx)
  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_trialname(trialIdx)
  ln_s(string(" block long 0-7 after the trial:"))
  ln_hex8(@chRec[trialIdx * BLKN])
  ln_s(string(" -> "))
  ln_s(lookupz(pat: string("right block"), string("long 0 the primer, longs 1-7 still the seed"), string("other")))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_trialname(trialIdx)
  ln_s(string(" completed: "))
  if st == ST_DONE
    ln_s(string("yes"))
  elseif st == ST_ECHO
    ln_s(string("yes, mode echo wrong (harness)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("NO - did not finish within 1 s (stopped)"))
  ln_s(string("; ping: "))
  if st == ST_LOST
    ln_s(string("not sent (trial not completed)"))
  elseif chAns[trialIdx]
    ln_s(string("answered within 100 ms; registers changed outside the sacrificial range and loop variables "))
    ln_d(chChanged[trialIdx])
    ln_s(string("; block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range "))
    ln_d(chStray[trialIdx])
    ln_s(string("; sacrificial range at the ping:"))
    ln_hex8(@chSac[trialIdx * BLKN])
  else
    ln_s(string("NO ANSWER within 100 ms (cog stopped)"))
  ln_out()

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' gates
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI is_clean(runIdx) : bClean
' @param runIdx - a run
' @returns bClean - every trial clean (R sentinel, PS right, B right block)

  bClean := runGoodAll[runIdx] == NTRIAL

PRI arm0_gate() : bPass | runIdx, kind, unwrCnt, otherCnt, disCnt
' Check arm 0's gates; print a line for each that fails.
'
' @returns bPass - TRUE when every gate of arm 0 passed

' Local Variables:
' @local runIdx - run index
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local unwrCnt - never-written records over the arm
' @local otherCnt - X values in the control runs
' @local disCnt - disagreeing cells over the arm

  bPass := TRUE
  unwrCnt := 0
  otherCnt := 0
  disCnt := 0
  repeat runIdx from RUN_C1 to RUN_T1F
    kind := run_fld(runIdx, RF_KIND)
    unwrCnt += runCnt[runIdx * NVC + VC_UNWR]
    disCnt += runDisagree[runIdx]
    if kind == KD_NOP or kind == KD_PS
      otherCnt += runOther[runIdx]
      if not is_clean(runIdx)
        ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): "))
        ln_runname(runIdx)
        ln_s(string(" (control) clean in "))
        ln_d(runGoodAll[runIdx])
        say(string(" of 1024 trials: the table, the addresses or the read path is wrong"))
        bPass := FALSE
  if unwrCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): "))
    ln_d(unwrCnt)
    say(string(" records still hold the fill $EEEE_EEEE: the measuring cog never wrote them"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if otherCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): "))
    ln_d(otherCnt)
    say(string(" values classified X (other) in a control run"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if disCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): "))
    ln_d(disCnt)
    say(string(" cells whose 16 repetitions disagree: the slot phase was not fixed"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if runRep0[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM] <> T1_PRED or not delta_match(RUN_T1) or runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM] <> T1_PRED * REPS or runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_SENT] <> T1_PRED_SENT * REPS
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): T1 k=0 did not reproduce EF-084: rep0 primer "))
    ln_d(runRep0[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" (MUST 43) by delta "))
    ln_row8(@runDelta[RUN_T1 * NSLOT])
    ln_s(string(" (MUST 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2); all reps primer "))
    ln_d(runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_PRIM])
    ln_s(string(" (MUST 688) sentinel "))
    ln_d(runCnt[RUN_T1 * NVC + VC_SENT])
    say(string(" (MUST 336)"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if not is_clean(RUN_T1F)
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): T1 k=7 sentinel in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[RUN_T1F])
    say(string(" of 1024 records (MUST 1024, EF-084 zero from k=7)"))
    bPass := FALSE
  if armDamage[ARM_P] > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE (arm 0): "))
    ln_d(armDamage[ARM_P])
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the arm (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))

PRI delta_match(runIdx) : bMatch | deltaIdx
' @param runIdx - run index
' @returns bMatch - TRUE when the run's repetition-0 delta split is 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2

' Local Variables:
' @local deltaIdx - delta 0..7

  bMatch := TRUE
  repeat deltaIdx from 0 to NSLOT - 1
    if runDelta[runIdx * NSLOT + deltaIdx] <> predK0[deltaIdx]
      bMatch := FALSE

PRI q_gate() : bPass | bIdx, rN
' Check arm 2's gates; print a line for each that fails, and the result.
'
' @returns bPass - TRUE when every gate of arm 2 passed

' Local Variables:
' @local bIdx - arm 2 slot
' @local rN - the NOP control run

  bPass := TRUE
  rN := RUN_Q + QS_N
  if qState[QS_N] <> ST_DONE or not is_clean(rN) or intChanged[QS_N] <> 0 or intStray[QS_N] <> 0
    ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm 2): QB N k0 (control): state "))
    ln_state(qState[QS_N])
    ln_s(string(", right block in "))
    ln_d(runGoodAll[rN])
    ln_s(string(" of 1024 records, registers changed outside the sacrificial range "))
    ln_d(intChanged[QS_N])
    ln_s(string(" (-1 = no copy), block/primer longs outside it "))
    ln_d(intStray[QS_N])
    say(string(" (MUST done, 1024, 0, 0)"))
    bPass := FALSE
  repeat bIdx from 0 to NBRUN - 1
    if qState[bIdx] == ST_ECHO
      ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm 2): mode echo mismatch in "))
      ln_runname(RUN_Q + bIdx)
      say(string(" (harness)"))
      bPass := FALSE
    if (qState[bIdx] == ST_DONE or qState[bIdx] == ST_LOST) and not qBaseOk[bIdx]
      ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm 2): the baseline cog-RAM copy of "))
      ln_runname(RUN_Q + bIdx)
      say(string(" did not equal the loaded image: its integrity check cannot be read"))
      bPass := FALSE
  if armDamage[ARM_Q] > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE (arm 2): "))
    ln_d(armDamage[ARM_Q])
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the arm (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))
  if bPass
    say(string("GATES PASS (arm 2): QB N k0 clean with cog RAM intact, every baseline equal to the loaded image, every mode echo right"))

PRI s_gate() : bPass | trialIdx
' Check arm 1's gates; print a line for each that fails, and the result.
'
' @returns bPass - TRUE when every gate of arm 1 passed

' Local Variables:
' @local trialIdx - arm 1 trial index

  bPass := TRUE
  repeat trialIdx from 0 to NCH - 1
    if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND) == KD_NOP and not ctl_ok(trialIdx)
      ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm 1): "))
      ln_trialname(trialIdx)
      ln_s(string(" (control): state "))
      ln_state(chState[trialIdx])
      ln_s(string(", answered "))
      ln_d(chAns[trialIdx] & 1)
      ln_s(string(", pattern "))
      ln_d(ch_pattern(trialIdx))
      ln_s(string(" (0 = right block), registers changed "))
      ln_d(chChanged[trialIdx])
      ln_s(string(", block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range "))
      ln_d(chStray[trialIdx])
      say(string(" (MUST done, answered 1, 0, 0, 0)"))
      bPass := FALSE
    if chState[trialIdx] == ST_ECHO
      ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm 1): mode echo mismatch in "))
      ln_trialname(trialIdx)
      say(string(" (harness)"))
      bPass := FALSE
    if (chState[trialIdx] == ST_DONE or chState[trialIdx] == ST_LOST) and not chBaseOk[trialIdx]
      ln_s(string("GATE FAIL (arm 1): the baseline cog-RAM copy of "))
      ln_trialname(trialIdx)
      say(string(" did not equal the loaded image: its integrity check cannot be read"))
      bPass := FALSE
  if armDamage[ARM_S] > 0
    ln_s(string("RIG NOTE (arm 1): "))
    ln_d(armDamage[ARM_S])
    say(string(" read-only data longs changed during the arm (see REGION DAMAGE lines)"))
  if bPass
    say(string("GATES PASS (arm 1): every NOP control trial right block, completed, answered, cog RAM intact; every baseline equal to the loaded image; every mode echo right"))

PRI rel_shown(trialIdx) : bShown | j, datum
' Arm 1: did this trial show a block read being released?  A released-cell
' test trial (EF-084 map P) shows it when its block has the primer in long
' 0, or a long left unwritten (the seed, or the record fill), or when its
' cog did not finish within 1 s (stopped).
'
' @param trialIdx - arm 1 trial index
' @returns bShown - TRUE when the trial showed a release

' Local Variables:
' @local j - long index
' @local datum - a block long

  bShown := FALSE
  if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND) <> KD_TEST or not ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_REL)
    return
  if chState[trialIdx] == ST_LOST
    bShown := TRUE
  if chState[trialIdx] == ST_LOST or chState[trialIdx] == ST_DONE or chState[trialIdx] == ST_ECHO
    if chRec[trialIdx * BLKN] == PRIMV
      bShown := TRUE
    repeat j from 0 to BLKN - 1
      datum := chRec[trialIdx * BLKN + j]
      if datum == SEEDV or datum == UNWRITTEN
        bShown := TRUE

PRI rel_count() : relCnt | trialIdx
' @returns relCnt - arm 1 trials that showed a block read being released

' Local Variables:
' @local trialIdx - arm 1 trial index

  relCnt := 0
  repeat trialIdx from 0 to NCH - 1
    if rel_shown(trialIdx)
      relCnt++

PRI ctl_ok(trialIdx) : bOk
' @param trialIdx - an arm 1 trial
' @returns bOk - TRUE when it completed, answered, recorded the right block,
'   and left cog RAM intact

  bOk := chState[trialIdx] == ST_DONE and chAns[trialIdx] and ch_pattern(trialIdx) == PAT_OK and chChanged[trialIdx] == 0 and chStray[trialIdx] == 0

PRI ln_state(st)
' Append the name of an ST_* state.
'
' @param st - ST_*

  ln_s(lookupz(st: string("not run"), string("cog did not start"), string("no baseline"), string("did not finish within 1 s (stopped)"), string("mode echo wrong"), string("done")))

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' verdicts
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_summary()
' Repeat every arm's verdict line, so the closing block holds them all.
'

  say(string("=== VERDICT SUMMARY (each arm's verdict as printed at its end; arms not completed say so) ==="))
  print_rig_line()
  observed_s()
  verdict_q(QS_C)
  verdict_q(QS_T6)
  verdict_q(QS_T7)
  verdict_q(QS_T8)

PRI ln_notdone(armIdx) : bNotDone
' If the arm did not complete, append the reason to the line, send it, and
' return TRUE.  The caller has already appended the verdict's name.
'
' @param armIdx - arm
' @returns bNotDone - TRUE when the arm did not complete (line sent)

  bNotDone := not armDone[armIdx]
  if bNotDone
    ln_s(string("NOT COMPLETED - the run ended before arm "))
    ln_d(armIdx)
    say(string(" ran (see the RIG FAIL line above)"))

PRI print_rig_line()
' Arm 0's verdict: RIG OK or RIG FAIL.
'

  if not armDone[ARM_P]
    say(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): arm 0 did not complete (see the RIG FAIL line above)"))
  elseif armPass[ARM_P]
    ln_s(string("RIG OK (arm 0, positive control): EF-084 reproduced - C1 sentinel and PS stream long in all 1024 records, T1 k=0 43 primer per repetition by delta 8 8 7 6 5 4 3 2 "))
    say(string("(688 primer, 336 sentinel), T1 k=7 sentinel in all 1024, no U, no X in a control, every cell's 16 repetitions identical"))
  else
    say(string("RIG FAIL (arm 0, positive control): EF-084 not reproduced (see the lines above) - no later verdict counts"))

PRI verdict_q(slot) | r, st, wrongCnt, unwrCnt, bLong, bReg, bCog, bUnknown
' VERDICT O29C BLOCK WAITING (QB C k0) / BLOCK k6 (QB T k6) / BLOCK k7 (QB T k7)
' / BLOCK k8 (QB T k8).
'
' @param slot - QS_C, QS_T6, QS_T7 or QS_T8

' Local Variables:
' @local r - the run
' @local st - its state
' @local wrongCnt - records written with a long that is not the right block
' @local unwrCnt - records never written
' @local bLong - part (a) holds
' @local bReg - part (b) holds
' @local bCog - part (c) holds
' @local bUnknown - part (b) could not be read

  r := RUN_Q + slot
  st := qState[slot]
  ln_s(lookupz(slot - QS_C: string("VERDICT O29C BLOCK WAITING: "), string("VERDICT O29C BLOCK k6: "), string("VERDICT O29C BLOCK k7: "), string("VERDICT O29C BLOCK k8: ")))
  if ln_notdone(ARM_Q)
    return
  if not armPass[ARM_P]
    say(string("NO VERDICT - arm 0 (positive control) failed: no later verdict counts; the rows above are raw"))
    return
  if not armPass[ARM_Q]
    say(string("NO VERDICT - a gate of arm 2 failed (see GATE FAIL lines); the rows above are raw"))
    return
  if st == ST_NOSTART or st == ST_NOBASE or st == ST_NOTRUN
    ln_s(string("NO VERDICT - the run did not take place ("))
    ln_state(st)
    say(string(")"))
    return
  unwrCnt := runCnt[r * NVC + BC_UNWR]
  bCog := st == ST_DONE and intChanged[slot] <> -1
  if st == ST_DONE
    wrongCnt := NTRIAL - runGoodAll[r]
  else
    wrongCnt := NTRIAL - runGoodAll[r] - unwrCnt
  bLong := wrongCnt == 0
  bUnknown := intChanged[slot] == -1
  bReg := not bUnknown and intChanged[slot] == 0 and intStray[slot] == 0
  if bLong and bReg and bCog
    if not armDone[ARM_S] or not armPass[ARM_S]
      ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - (a), (b), (c) held, but a gate of arm 1 failed, so its release evidence cannot be read and a clean workaround run proves nothing without it"))
    elseif rel_count() == 0
      ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - the rig did not show a block read being released (characterisation arm), so a clean workaround run proves nothing; (a), (b), (c) held"))
    else
      ln_s(string("CONFIRMED - the right block in 1024 of 1024 records, 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range and no block or primer long outside it, the cog completed the run; arm 1 showed a release in "))
      ln_d(rel_count())
      ln_s(string(" trials"))
  elseif not bLong or (not bUnknown and not bReg) or st == ST_LOST
    ln_s(string("REFUTED -"))
    if not bLong
      ln_s(string(" wrong long: "))
      ln_d(wrongCnt)
      ln_s(string(" of 1024 records written with a long that is not the right block (primer-in-record "))
      ln_d(runCnt[r * NVC + BC_PRIM])
      ln_s(string(", seed-in-record "))
      ln_d(runCnt[r * NVC + BC_SEED])
      ln_s(string(", both "))
      ln_d(runCnt[r * NVC + BC_MIX])
      ln_s(string(", other "))
      ln_d(runCnt[r * NVC + BC_OTHER])
      if st == ST_DONE
        ln_s(string(", unwritten "))
        ln_d(unwrCnt)
      ln_s(string(");"))
    if not bUnknown and not bReg
      ln_s(string(" register change: "))
      ln_d(intChanged[slot])
      ln_s(string(" cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range"))
      if intChanged[slot] > 0
        ln_s(string(" (first "))
        ln_hx(intFirst[slot], 3)
        ln_c(")")
      ln_s(string(", "))
      ln_d(intStray[slot])
      ln_s(string(" block/primer longs outside it;"))
    if st == ST_LOST
      ln_s(string(" did not finish within 1 s (stopped): records never written "))
      ln_d(unwrCnt)
      ln_s(string("; cog RAM not checked (no copy)"))
  else
    ln_s(string("INCONCLUSIVE - every record right, but the cog completed without its cog-RAM copy arriving: part (b) could not be read"))
  ln_out()
  say(string("  written before the run: CONFIRMED = the right block $5A5A_0100+ar+j in all 1024 records, 0 cog registers changed outside the sacrificial range, the cog completes the run, and arm 1 showed a release (else INCONCLUSIVE);"))
  say(string("  REFUTED = wrong long / register change / did not finish within 1 s (stopped), each named"))

PRI observed_s() | trialIdx, kind, pat, nCtlOk, nEscRun, nEscOk, nRelRun, nRelOk, nRelP1, nRelOth, nTried, nDone, nAns, nAnsRel, nAnsEsc, nChg, nStray, relCnt
' OBSERVED O29C SETQ k0 (records): the main line, one line per cell, one
' line of ping and cog-RAM results.  Every line stays under LINE_MAX.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local trialIdx - arm 1 trial index
' @local kind - KD_*
' @local pat - PAT_*
' @local nCtlOk - control trials passing
' @local nEscRun - escaping-cell test trials run
' @local nEscOk - of them, the right block
' @local nRelRun - released-cell test trials run
' @local nRelOk - of them, the right block
' @local nRelP1 - of them, long 0 the primer and longs 1-7 the seed
' @local nRelOth - of them, other
' @local nTried - test trials run
' @local nDone - test trials completed
' @local nAns - test trials whose cog answered the ping
' @local nAnsRel - released-cell trials answered
' @local nAnsEsc - escaping-cell trials answered
' @local nChg - answered test trials with registers changed
' @local nStray - block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range, over the answered test trials
' @local relCnt - trials that showed a block read being released

  ln_s(string("OBSERVED O29C SETQ k0: "))
  if ln_notdone(ARM_S)
    return
  nCtlOk := 0
  nEscRun := 0
  nEscOk := 0
  nRelRun := 0
  nRelOk := 0
  nRelP1 := 0
  nRelOth := 0
  nTried := 0
  nDone := 0
  nAns := 0
  nAnsRel := 0
  nAnsEsc := 0
  nChg := 0
  nStray := 0
  repeat trialIdx from 0 to NCH - 1
    kind := ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND)
    if kind == KD_NOP
      if ctl_ok(trialIdx)
        nCtlOk++
    elseif chState[trialIdx] == ST_LOST or chState[trialIdx] == ST_DONE or chState[trialIdx] == ST_ECHO
      nTried++
      pat := ch_pattern(trialIdx)
      if chState[trialIdx] <> ST_LOST
        nDone++
      if chAns[trialIdx]
        nAns++
        if chChanged[trialIdx] > 0
          nChg++
        nStray += chStray[trialIdx]
      if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_REL)
        nRelRun++
        if chAns[trialIdx]
          nAnsRel++
        if pat == PAT_OK
          nRelOk++
        elseif pat == PAT_P1
          nRelP1++
        else
          nRelOth++
      else
        nEscRun++
        if chAns[trialIdx]
          nAnsEsc++
        if pat == PAT_OK
          nEscOk++
  if not armPass[ARM_P]
    ln_s(string("NO VERDICT - arm 0 (positive control) failed; raw counts: "))
  elseif not armPass[ARM_S]
    ln_s(string("NO VERDICT - a gate of arm 1 failed (see GATE FAIL lines); raw counts: "))
  ln_s(string("escaping cells (af0/ar4, af1/ar3): right block in "))
  ln_d(nEscOk)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(nEscRun)
  ln_s(string(" trials run; released cells (af0/ar0, af2/ar0): right block "))
  ln_d(nRelOk)
  ln_s(string(", long 0 the primer with longs 1-7 still the seed "))
  ln_d(nRelP1)
  ln_s(string(", other "))
  ln_d(nRelOth)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(nRelRun)
  ln_s(string(" run; completed "))
  ln_d(nDone)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(nTried)
  relCnt := rel_count()
  if relCnt > 0
    ln_s(string("; RELEASE SHOWN: yes, in "))
    ln_d(relCnt)
    ln_s(string(" released-cell trials"))
  else
    ln_s(string("; RELEASE SHOWN: no"))
  ln_out()
  repeat trialIdx from 0 to NCH - 1
    if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND) == KD_NOP
      ln_cell_line(trialIdx)
  ln_s(string("  OBSERVED O29C SETQ k0 cog: the cog answered the ping afterwards in "))
  ln_d(nAns)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(nTried)
  ln_s(string(" (released cells "))
  ln_d(nAnsRel)
  ln_s(string(", escaping cells "))
  ln_d(nAnsEsc)
  ln_s(string("); answered trials with registers changed outside the sacrificial range and loop variables "))
  ln_d(nChg)
  ln_s(string(", block/primer longs outside the sacrificial range "))
  ln_d(nStray)
  ln_s(string(" | NOP controls clean "))
  ln_d(nCtlOk)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(NCELL_S)
  ln_out()

PRI ln_cell_line(ctlIdx) | trialIdx, afIdx, arIdx, nCellRun, nOk, nP1, nOth, nDone, nAns
' Print one characterised cell's OBSERVED line: its test trials by block
' pattern, completed, answered.
'
' @param ctlIdx - the cell's NOP control trial (gives af, ar, class)

' Local Variables:
' @local trialIdx - arm 1 trial index
' @local afIdx - the cell's stream slot bits
' @local arIdx - the cell's block slot bits
' @local nCellRun - its test trials run
' @local nOk - of them, the right block
' @local nP1 - of them, long 0 the primer and longs 1-7 the seed
' @local nOth - of them, other
' @local nDone - of them, completed
' @local nAns - of them, answered the ping

  afIdx := ch_fld(ctlIdx, CF_AF)
  arIdx := ch_fld(ctlIdx, CF_AR)
  nCellRun := 0
  nOk := 0
  nP1 := 0
  nOth := 0
  nDone := 0
  nAns := 0
  repeat trialIdx from 0 to NCH - 1
    if ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_KIND) == KD_TEST and ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AF) == afIdx and ch_fld(trialIdx, CF_AR) == arIdx
      if chState[trialIdx] == ST_LOST or chState[trialIdx] == ST_DONE or chState[trialIdx] == ST_ECHO
        nCellRun++
        if chState[trialIdx] <> ST_LOST
          nDone++
        if chAns[trialIdx]
          nAns++
        if ch_pattern(trialIdx) == PAT_OK
          nOk++
        elseif ch_pattern(trialIdx) == PAT_P1
          nP1++
        else
          nOth++
  ln_s(string("  OBSERVED O29C SETQ k0 cell af"))
  ln_d(afIdx)
  ln_s(string("/ar"))
  ln_d(arIdx)
  if ch_fld(ctlIdx, CF_REL)
    ln_s(string(" (released, P)"))
  else
    ln_s(string(" (escaping, S)"))
  ln_s(string(": right block "))
  ln_d(nOk)
  ln_s(string(", long 0 the primer with longs 1-7 still the seed "))
  ln_d(nP1)
  ln_s(string(", other "))
  ln_d(nOth)
  ln_s(string(" of "))
  ln_d(nCellRun)
  ln_s(string(" run; completed "))
  ln_d(nDone)
  ln_s(string(", answered the ping "))
  ln_d(nAns)
  ln_s(string(" | NOP control clean "))
  ln_d(ctl_ok(ctlIdx) & 1)
  ln_out()

DAT ' ---- Fixed predictions and the run tables ----
' EF-084: primer cells per repetition at k=0, by delta 0..7
predK0          long    8, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2

' Run table, in run order: arm, shape, kind, copy, no-wait, k.
runTab          byte    ARM_P,  SH_R,  KD_NOP,  CP_R_NOP_L,  0, 0      '  0 C1
                byte    ARM_P,  SH_PS, KD_PS,   CP_R_PS,     1, 0      '  1 PS
                byte    ARM_P,  SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF0_L,  1, 0      '  2 T1 k=0
                byte    ARM_P,  SH_R,  KD_TEST, CP_R_RF7_L,  1, 7      '  3 T1 k=7
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_NOP,  CP_B_NOP,    0, 0      '  4 QB N k0
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_WAIT, CP_B_RF0,    0, 0      '  5 QB C k0 (waiting form)
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_TEST, CP_B_RF6,    1, 6      '  6 QB T k6 (E8's rule exactly: 16 clocks)
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_TEST, CP_B_RF7,    1, 7      '  7 QB T k7
                byte    ARM_Q,  SH_B,  KD_TEST, CP_B_RF8,    1, 8      '  8 QB T k8
runTabEnd       byte    0

' Arm 1 trial table, in trial order: kind, af, ar, class in the EF-084 map
' (1 released P, 0 escaping S).  The NOP controls first, one per cell.
chTab           byte    KD_NOP,  0, 0, 1                                '  0 QS N af0 ar0 (control)
                byte    KD_NOP,  0, 4, 0                                '  1 QS N af0 ar4 (control)
                byte    KD_NOP,  2, 0, 1                                '  2 QS N af2 ar0 (control)
                byte    KD_NOP,  1, 3, 0                                '  3 QS N af1 ar3 (control)
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 0, 1                                '  4 QS T af0 ar0 #1 (released: af0 PPPSSSSS)
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 0, 1
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 0, 1
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 0, 1
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 4, 0                                '  8 QS T af0 ar4 #1 (escaping: af0 PPPSSSSS)
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 4, 0
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 4, 0
                byte    KD_TEST, 0, 4, 0
                byte    KD_TEST, 2, 0, 1                                ' 12 QS T af2 ar0 #1 (released: af2 PPPPPPPP)
                byte    KD_TEST, 2, 0, 1
                byte    KD_TEST, 2, 0, 1
                byte    KD_TEST, 2, 0, 1
                byte    KD_TEST, 1, 3, 0                                ' 16 QS T af1 ar3 #1 (escaping: af1 SPPSSSSS)
                byte    KD_TEST, 1, 3, 0
                byte    KD_TEST, 1, 3, 0
                byte    KD_TEST, 1, 3, 0
chTabEnd        byte    0
                alignl

' ===========================================================================
' MEASURING COG (PASM, cog exec).  PTRA on entry = @mbox (from COGINIT).
' No debug(), no BRK, no interrupt in this cog (DEBUG_COGS excludes it), and
' no ## operand anywhere.  From each primer RDLONG to its test instruction
' there is nothing but the RDFAST (or the NOP standing in for it), the k
' NOPs and (block) the SETQ.  Loop variables are grouped (c_cmd..c_tmp);
' the sacrificial block registers and their guard bands end the image.
' ===========================================================================
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Cog ----
pasm            rdfast  #0, c_strm                              ' FIFO pre-conditioning: blocking, streams from the stream region
                mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
st_d0           djnz    c_t, #st_d0                             ' the FIFO full and idle, as after any trial
                wrlong  c_ready, ptra[MB_ALIVE]                 ' start-up handshake

wait_cmd        rdlong  c_cmd, ptra                     wz      ' MB_CMD: 0 = idle
        if_z    jmp     #wait_cmd
                rdlong  c_copy, ptra[MB_COPY]
                rdlong  c_mode, ptra[MB_MODE]
                rdlong  c_af1, ptra[MB_AF]
                rdlong  c_ar1, ptra[MB_AR]
                rdlong  c_pa, ptra[MB_PRIM]
                rdlong  c_tb, ptra[MB_TBL]
                alts    c_copy, #vec_tab
                mov     c_vec, 0-0
                mov     c_rp, c_res
                mov     c_reps, #REPS
                mov     c_one, #0
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_R                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #r_rep
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_B                   wz
        if_z    jmp     #b_rep
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_B1                  wz
        if_z    jmp     #b1_ent
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_SNAP                wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_snap
                cmp     c_cmd, #CMD_PING                wz
        if_z    jmp     #do_ping
cmd_done        wrlong  c_mode, ptra[MB_ECHO]                   ' epilogue, after every record: echo the mode run
                wrlong  #0, ptra                                ' MB_CMD := 0 -> done
                jmp     #wait_cmd

do_snap         setq    #COG_DUMP_N - 1                         ' baseline: cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub
                wrlong  pasm, c_dump
                jmp     #cmd_done

do_ping         setq    #COG_DUMP_N - 1                         ' ping: cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub, then the answer
                wrlong  pasm, c_dump
                wrlong  c_pong, ptra[MB_ALIVE]
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- settle: >= 200 clocks.  Changes no flag.
settle          mov     c_t, #SETTLE_N
s_d1            djnz    c_t, #s_d1
                ret

'--- image R: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 ar; record (rep*8 + af)*8 + ar
r_rep           mov     c_af, #0
r_af            mov     c_ar, #0
r_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm                            ' stream address: slot bits = af
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tb                              ' test address: slot bits = ar
                mov     c_dst, c_seedv                          ' "never written" stays visible
                jmp     c_vec                                   ' the trial copy
r_settle        call    #settle
                wrlong  c_dst, c_rp                             ' one record per trial
                add     c_rp, #4
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #r_af
                djnz    c_reps, #r_rep
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- block: 16 repetitions x 8 af x 8 ar; record blk0..blk7 per trial
'--- (CMD_B1: one trial at af = MB_AF, ar = MB_AR, one record, no integrity copy)
b1_ent          mov     c_af, c_af1
                mov     c_ar, c_ar1
                mov     c_one, #1
                jmp     #b_ar
b_rep           mov     c_af, #0
b_af            mov     c_ar, #0
b_ar            mov     c_pf, c_af
                shl     c_pf, #2
                add     c_pf, c_strm
                mov     c_pr, c_ar
                shl     c_pr, #2
                add     c_pr, c_tb                              ' block start: slot bits = ar
                mov     c_blk0 + 0, c_seedv                     ' the sacrificial range := seed
                mov     c_blk0 + 1, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 2, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 3, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 4, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 5, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 6, c_seedv
                mov     c_blk0 + 7, c_seedv
                jmp     c_vec
b_settle        call    #settle
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                wrlong  c_blk0, c_rp                            ' record: the 8 sacrificial longs
                add     c_rp, #BLKN * 4
                tjnz    c_one, #cmd_done                        ' CMD_B1: done after its one record
                add     c_ar, #1
                cmp     c_ar, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #b_ar
                add     c_af, #1
                cmp     c_af, #NSLOT                    wz
        if_nz   jmp     #b_af
                djnz    c_reps, #b_rep
                setq    #COG_DUMP_N - 1                         ' integrity: cog RAM $000-$1EF to hub
                wrlong  pasm, c_dump
                jmp     #cmd_done

'--- image R trial copies: primer, RDFAST (or NOP), k NOPs, the read under test
tc_r_nop_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' primer
                nop                                             ' NOP in place of the RDFAST
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr                             ' the RDLONG under test
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_rf0_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_rf7_l      rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                rdlong  c_dst, c_pr
                jmp     #r_settle
tc_r_ps         rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' PS: primer
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf                            ' PS: the stream under test (no-wait)
                waitx   #STREAM_WAIT                            ' PS: long past any start-up
                rflong  c_dst                                   ' PS: the stream's first long
                jmp     #r_settle

'--- block copies: primer, RDFAST (or NOP), k NOPs, SETQ + the block RDLONG
tc_b_nop        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                nop
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr                            ' the block RDLONG under test
                jmp     #b_settle
tc_b_rf0        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr
                jmp     #b_settle
tc_b_rf6        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa                             ' E8's rule exactly: 6 NOPs + SETQ = 7 non-hub instructions
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr
                jmp     #b_settle
tc_b_rf7        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr
                jmp     #b_settle
tc_b_rf8        rdlong  c_tmp, c_pa
                rdfast  c_mode, c_pf
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                nop
                setq    #BLKN - 1
                rdlong  c_blk0, c_pr
                jmp     #b_settle

'--- trial-copy vectors (CP_* order)
vec_tab         long    tc_r_nop_l, tc_r_rf0_l, tc_r_rf7_l, tc_r_ps             ' 0..3
                long    tc_b_nop, tc_b_rf0, tc_b_rf6, tc_b_rf7, tc_b_rf8        ' 4..8

'--- cog constants
c_strm          long    HUB_STRM
c_res           long    HUB_RES
c_dump          long    HUB_DUMP
c_seedv         long    SEEDV
c_ready         long    STAT_READY
c_pong          long    STAT_PONG

'--- loop variables (c_cmd .. c_tmp): excluded from the "changed" check
c_cmd           long    0
c_copy          long    0
c_mode          long    0                                       ' FIFO D under test
c_af1           long    0                                       ' CMD_B1: af
c_ar1           long    0                                       ' CMD_B1: ar
c_pa            long    0
c_tb            long    0
c_vec           long    0
c_rp            long    0
c_reps          long    0
c_one           long    0                                       ' 1: CMD_B1 single trial
c_af            long    0
c_ar            long    0
c_pf            long    0
c_pr            long    0
c_dst           long    0
c_t             long    0
c_tmp           long    0                                       ' the primer read's destination

'--- guard band, the sacrificial range (written only by the block reads and
'--- their presets), guard band; checked except the sacrificial range
c_guard_lo      long    GUARD_V + 0, GUARD_V + 1, GUARD_V + 2, GUARD_V + 3, GUARD_V + 4, GUARD_V + 5, GUARD_V + 6, GUARD_V + 7
c_blk0          long    0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
c_guard_hi      long    GUARD_V + 8, GUARD_V + 9, GUARD_V + 10, GUARD_V + 11, GUARD_V + 12, GUARD_V + 13, GUARD_V + 14, GUARD_V + 15
pasm_end

